{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves","id":1114913,"title":"Vampires vs. Werewolves!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-11T21:42:06-07:00","id":1114913,"title":"Vampires vs. Werewolves!","content":"In NWoD, I have never actually had or seen werewolves fight vampires. How is it? I have seen plenty of vampire vs. werewolf fights in VtM, which usually didn't turn out well for the vampires. What's it like? And why do they fight if they did? WtF virtually has nothing on vampires or even VtR. It's out of the a werewolf's scope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T22:57:10-07:00","id":1114939,"title":"","content":"Are you reading 2e? Because a starting werewolf could easily tear through a starting coterie under the current rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T23:17:57-07:00","id":1114955,"title":"","content":"Unlike VtM &amp; WtA, there is no mechanic or fluff reason for the two splats to want to box every time they run into each other. In fact the whole Chod is very non-splat antagonistic in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T00:53:52-07:00","id":1114969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1114955#post1114955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact the whole Chod is very non-splat antagonistic in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Rather, <i>CoD</i> universe assumes that monster races do not have one answer to other monsters. </b>Your particular Uratha or a Pack can hate vampires from deaths of all it hearts - it's just werewolf race as all do not have one answer. We have Siberian Lodge <i>Eaters of Dead</i> that hunt <b>only</b> vampires ( see book <b>The Pack</b> to 2E for them ). We have <b><i>whole</i> Tribe</b> putting other monsters hiding inside humanity as Sacred Prey - Iron Masters - or some Tribes that often mistake other monsters for other threats - like Storm Lords, thinking changelings or vampires are some kind of Spirits Claimed. Examples on those are in 2E Tribes stereotypes and <i>Wolf &amp; Raven</i> Dark Era ( i.e. Viking times setting ). It's simply is not 'all Uratha hunt vampires' stereotype across whole race.<br /> <br /> In fact, in my own <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1080206-2e-hunting-grounds-uppsala-sweden\">Uppsala, Sweden fan setting</a> tense ( and probable conflict ) relations with vampire rule of Archbishop of city is one of major themes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-12-2017, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T03:11:49-07:00","id":1114999,"title":"","content":"In my 2e vampire campaign werewolves were fun and/or terrifying depending on whether you'd crossed them or not. Vampires and wolves lived in the same city, their territories overlapped in many ways and there was a diplomatic position under the city's prince that dealt with &quot;negotiating&quot; and &quot;being an ambassador&quot; to the werewolves. The various tensions were constantly messy. <br /> <br /> This meant trying to delicately avoid an all out fight when a vampire had pissed off a werewolf. (Usually by messing up their territory, killing their favorite old lady who brings in happy flower spirits, buying up a corner bar that's their favorite drinking spot and turning it into a hunting ground.)<br /> <br /> Or trying to get some kind of &quot;demonstration of remorse&quot; when a vampire had pissed off a werewolf then been utterly destroyed/eaten by said werewolf and pack before any kind of negotiations had taken place.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, werewolves were very tempting blood dolls and body guards for many a vampire, if you could maneuver them into cooperating with that. And an influential vampire could lend a stabilizing support to a weak pack trying to establish itself.<br /> <br /> As far as fighting, I think almost any vampire was at a serious disadvantage against a pack who was hunting them. Being asleep half the day pretty much ensures you're going to get tracked and killed at some point while you're vulnerable. The best way to go against them was to anonymously recruit another werewolf pack. <br /> <br /> I highly recommend werewolves in any vampire game, it keeps the vampires a little humble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T03:21:42-07:00","id":1115002,"title":"","content":"This again? And why is it always always always in the werewolf forum? <br /> <br /> Every game line has its niche. With the exception of Mage (who are basically OP), every game excells in that niche. Vampires are best at mind controls, social-fu, and cooersion. Werewolves are best at a hunt. You run a game that focuses on hunting and physical challeges, werewolves come out ahead. Something more social where vampire mind controls, cooercion, blood bonds and more come into play? They have the advantage.<br /> <br /> And that's not even touching on the fact that werewolves have spirit allies, nor that its not one pack versus one cotorie, its a pack versus the vampire covenants - favor trading and status can be nasty. The two games are just too different to have a meaningful, objective comparison.<br /> <br /> And start worryin' about hunting some mages, or prommies, or beasts. The Begotten go around creating fear and destruction spirits and mess up people's lives for the sake of feeding their sadistic hungers. They're pretty nasty to the balance of territory. Why not talk about them some? There's an entire Kuruth Trigger for meeting anything but a normal human or another werewolf type. Werewolves have no reason to focus on vampires especially in the CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-12-2017, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T04:13:50-07:00","id":1115017,"title":"","content":"From my own very very limited experience with Werewolf players fighting Vampire NPC's in 2E (basically only one fight so far) Vampires have no chance in a &quot;fair&quot; fight, as in going toe-to-toe against even a newly changed Werewolf in melee. The only chance they seem to have is if the Werewolf has already done their 1-Gauru-change-per-scene and they don't go into Death Rage and you have a very powerful Elder Vampire full of blood.<br /> <br /> Or you do enough damage in 1 hit to pretty much insta-kill. I recommend being an expert marksman with an anti-material sniper rifle, firing at a human form Werewolf in the head from 300m away. And then rolling really lucky, hoping you do enough damage to stun, then shoot them again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:07:57-07:00","id":1115033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves#post1114913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In NWoD, I have never actually had or seen werewolves fight vampires. How is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick and brutal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have seen plenty of vampire vs. werewolf fights in VtM, which usually didn't turn out well for the vampires. </div> </div> </div>As you probably noticed from other posts, there's no real inbuilt reason for werewolves to hunt vampires the way they did in Masquerade, where vampires were touched by the Wyrm and sort of walked around with werewolf targets on their back. That said, it does happen. There's a would-be tribe, currently in lodge form as the Eaters of the Dead, that is dedicated to it, and individual packs can set a focus to hunt whatever they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's it like? And why do they fight if they did? </div> </div> </div>Werewolves can choose to hunt vampires for all manner of reasons, of course. Ranging from simply not liking them or a personal vendetta like they killed his family and forced his First Change to something obscure like they rendered a locus unusable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WtF virtually has nothing on vampires or even VtR. It's out of the a werewolf's scope. </div> </div> </div>We're expecting a Crossover book in a while that might cover this sort of thing. Meanwhile, the Pack does have some information about vampire and werewolf interactions, but it's mostly from the point of vampires being in a werewolf's pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-12-2017, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:11:28-07:00","id":1115080,"title":"","content":"It's kind of the nuclear option, but at their peak, &quot;set literally everything within a ten mile radius of me on fire&quot; is something a werewolf could potentially do. <br /> <br /> So, yeah, going to war would end badly for the vamps. Minor skirmishes though? That can go either way. Always pays to remember that a vampire's real forte is <i>avoiding</i> a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T09:05:33-07:00","id":1115107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115033#post1115033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you probably noticed from other posts, there's no real inbuilt reason for werewolves to hunt vampires the way they did in Masquerade, where vampires were touched by the Wyrm and sort of walked around with werewolf targets on their back. That said, it does happen. There's a would-be tribe, currently in lodge form as the Eaters of the Dead, that is dedicated to it, and individual packs can set a focus to hunt whatever they want.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of what I have noticed since the WtA-days. There's no reason for a werewolf to hunt vampires other than any reason a vampre would have to hunt vampires. However, it's a big theme of VtM and VtR games. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T09:48:33-07:00","id":1115121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115107#post1115107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it's a big theme of VtM and VtR games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it's a big thing in Requiem's setting, so if it's a big thing in their games it may just be the storyteller. I often run them as uneasy allies in the dark, since their lifestyles, compared to the other gamelines, are so close. They're both predators and occasionally kill other members of their own kind and humans, but they're also the only ones who are really 'tagged' by the media. If someone discovered a Changeling with their Masque down they would likely have no idea what to think of the green man with the horns. But a man that shifts into a wolf is likely a werewolf, and a woman drinking blood with her fangs from a woman is likely a vampire, and there's a whole slew of easy-to-access movies telling you how to deal with it, even if they aren't 100% correct.<br /> <br /> They're the big two, most numerous and popular, and since their activities cause them to have to have a 'normal' second life, they run into each other a lot in the course of it. If it always flipped to combat just because a vampire lived on the same block as a werewolf, life as either would be untenable. So there's more of an appreciation for each other as creatures of the dark.<br /> <br /> The tremendous weakness of Daysleep gives a big incentive for vampires to not instigate fights, and werewolves don't exactly want to lose their friends or family. In my last game my werewolf's best friend fell into a vampire crowd while he was digging into something else. When he was blood bonded he just wasn't the same person, so I made an agreement with the vampiress who did it in exchange for her letting him go and skipping town, never to be seen again. It ended up with my character taking out a house of ghouls, sneaking into secret dugout basement with living plants, getting lost in the secret exit before trailing back and finding the sleeping vampire and staking then destroying them. It was done during the day, but it was way outside of our territory, and the vampires were very organized in this place, verging on breaking the masquerade they had such open control over things, so it was very risky, especially since the ghouls were armed with silver bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:37:23-07:00","id":1115135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1114969#post1114969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Rather, <i>CoD</i> universe assumes that monster races do not have one answer to other monsters. </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Your particular Uratha or a Pack can hate vampires from deaths of all it hearts - it's just werewolf race as all do not have one answer. We have Siberian Lodge <i>Eaters of Dead</i> that hunt <b>only</b> vampires ( see book <b>The Pack</b> to 2E for them ). We have <b><i>whole</i> Tribe</b> putting other monsters hiding inside humanity as Sacred Prey - Iron Masters - or some Tribes that often mistake other monsters for other threats - like Storm Lords, thinking changelings or vampires are some kind of Spirits Claimed. Examples on those are in 2E Tribes stereotypes and <i>Wolf &amp; Raven</i> Dark Era ( i.e. Viking times setting ). It's simply is not 'all Uratha hunt vampires' stereotype across whole race.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In fact, in my own <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1080206-2e-hunting-grounds-uppsala-sweden\">Uppsala, Sweden fan setting</a> tense ( and probable conflict ) relations with vampire rule of Archbishop of city is one of major themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>and lets not forget <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Shadows_of_Mexico\" target=\"_blank\">Shadows over Mexico</a>, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1103084-sublunario-dead-wolves-2e#post1103084\">Dead Wolves</a> for the opposite end of the spectrum.<br /> <br /> In my Portland Oregon Setting the most powerful Seers of the Throne Pylon has an alliance with the current Carthian Vampire rulers, and the local Pure and Forsaken have an uneasy truce, making the Uratha and Vampire situation an potentially volitile situation if the Vampires push buttons that'd make they good targets for a Sacred Hunt, but also makes several areas known to be dangerous to the Uratha (like to World Trade Center, a Elysium and where the Pylon play host to other Seers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-12-2017, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:32:05-07:00","id":1115155,"title":"","content":"I think there a have been a couple of hints that the Pure tend not to get along with vampires. The Blood Talons' line about vampires is &quot;Creepy dead bastards do half our work for us&quot; and the Dead Jacks and the werewolves of the Gower are at each others' throats. Maybe vampires tend to piss off the Hisil or the Ivory Claws have a bone to pick with them. I could see a few Circle of the Crone covens buddying up with Bale Hounds or Predator Kings though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:36:45-07:00","id":1115157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115155#post1115155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see a few Circle of the Crone covens buddying up with Bale Hounds or Predator Kings though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you say that! My friend uses Crone/Predator King packs so often they are frequently called the Pure Crone in his games and Hunters in the area are confused as to the line between vampires and werewolves (Many Gangrel Dead Wolves in the wilderness near his cities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:43:00-07:00","id":1115160,"title":"","content":"That makes sense.<br /> <br /> The Pure were more fanatical in first edition, it was hard to imagine them 'grouping' with anyone playing them completely by the book, but the changes in second really make them a more plausible for that. The Ivory Claws are definitely going to bump heads with the Invictus, going back and forth between warring and allying, the Predator Kings and Crone fit so well especially for a huntress-based cult of them, that's some great imagery Pale_Crusader. I could see the Circle with the Fire-Touched, too, if they were a particularly spiritual coven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:44:38-07:00","id":1115161,"title":"","content":"Typically when it comes to vampires versus werewolves, the vampire part of the equation typically loses, whether it be social or physical. In physical combat it's obvious, but for social I remember playing a social vampire and the werewolf's spirit gifts kind of outdid me. Really, a vampire's real specialty is the ammount of merits they can get over the ages. Vampires can be very deeply entrenched in mortal society, and they can have allies anywhere. And if a werewolf pack takes on a vampire, they might be dealing with the vampire's covenant mates.<br /> <br /> So in general, a vampire could win with prep time, but a werewolf with prep time is also dangerous, so they could win. Also, a werewolf dropping a fire spirit into the vampire's haven is a dick movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":". 07-12-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T13:00:28-07:00","id":1115210,"title":"","content":"Vampires are leeches.<br /> <br /> They don't care about anything but the next meal. They're murderous little parasites that create death spirits wherever they go; Luna help you if you find one digging its fangs into someone (or someones) in your territory, because they're goddamn kudzu: even if you kill one, she might just come back anyway. Fighting? Hah. Easy enough. Fire and gasoline, light 'em up and let God sort 'em out...but they can breed like rabbits. Their taint can turn even your kin, those Wolf-Blooded you rely so much on. Imagine everyone you ever loved in utter thrall to a dead thing, and you'll only scratch the surface of what they can do to you. Fighting doesn't matter if they won't let you do it.<br /> <br /> If you must fight, and pray to Urfarah you never do, you're going to have to eradicate them. Salt the earth. Offer no quarter.<br /> <br /> <i>...Except </i>if you need one.<br /> <br /> If you need a vampire, it's the only thing that'll do. What werewolf do you know that can erase memories, read minds, charm whole crowds, and spread fear like a plague? A single night and a drop of Vitae here and there, and those fuckos at the Parks Board will stay the hell away from the locus you've been trying to protect with protests for the last eight months. Need to hide something? They don't call it a Masquerade for nothing. Need the kind of blood magic the petty lords of the Shadow won't know the first thing about? They can do it for you wholesale.<br /> <br /> So really, try not to need one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 07-12-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:09:35-07:00","id":1115245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115157#post1115157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny you say that! My friend uses Crone/Predator King packs so often they are frequently called the Pure Crone in his games and Hunters in the area are confused as to the line between vampires and werewolves (Many Gangrel Dead Wolves in the wilderness near his cities).</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the idea after reading a suggestion on the recent Crone thread that they could have influence over gangs in particular. You know where a young and successful Pure Crone would fit in beautifully? Streets of Rage. Think about it. A modern glass and steel city, full of neon and other sources of light pollution, turned feral with thugs using the whole place as their playground. And I think the panache of the setting would be something that the Circle could get behind, especially in defiance of a more austere Lancea et Sanctum. But that's more of a topic for the other thread, if either of these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:12:01-07:00","id":1115249,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> At first, I wasn't sure to be on board with said analysis, but then I looked at it from a werewolf's perspective and promptly agreed.<br /> <br /> Also, can't werewolves mess with whole organizations with spirit magic? So why couldn't they do that with the Parks Board?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:16:31-07:00","id":1115251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115249#post1115249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> At first, I wasn't sure to be on board with said analysis, but then I looked at it from a werewolf's perspective and promptly agreed.<br /> <br /> Also, can't werewolves mess with whole organizations with spirit magic? So why couldn't they do that with the Parks Board?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm being slightly facetious for dramatic effect; there's plenty of spirit magic that could do the job, I just tend to think of spirit magic being a lot more contractual and give-and-take. A vampire'll do it because she's bored...though you'd probably owe her too, if setting her up with a bunch of thralls weren't enough... But then, like I said, try not to need one.<br /> <br /> Edit: And really, my analysis is from a far more conservative werewolf perspective. There are plenty of Uratha who'd be like &quot;So you can mind wipe my enemies and all I have to do is let you have a sip of blood? Rad!&quot; (Those ones don't live long.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T16:41:36-07:00","id":1115296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115251#post1115251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'm being slightly facetious for dramatic effect; there's plenty of spirit magic that could do the job, I just tend to think of spirit magic being a lot more contractual and give-and-take. A vampire'll do it because she's bored...though you'd probably owe her too, if setting her up with a bunch of thralls weren't enough... But then, like I said, try not to need one.<br /> <br /> Edit: And really, my analysis is from a far more conservative werewolf perspective. There are plenty of Uratha who'd be like &amp;quot;So you can mind wipe my enemies and all I have to do is let you have a sip of blood? Rad!&amp;quot; (Those ones don't live long.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally the werewolf games I've been in have had the pack breaks oaths with the vampire coterie and hunting them down with lots of murder involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:33:18-07:00","id":1115381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115245#post1115245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got the idea after reading a suggestion on the recent Crone thread that they could have influence over gangs in particular. You know where a young and successful Pure Crone would fit in beautifully? Streets of Rage. Think about it. A modern glass and steel city, full of neon and other sources of light pollution, turned feral with thugs using the whole place as their playground. And I think the panache of the setting would be something that the Circle could get behind, especially in defiance of a more austere Lancea et Sanctum. But that's more of a topic for the other thread, if either of these.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not Predator Kings not jive with that on basista their Tribal Ban stoping them from entering city or using things in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:50:24-07:00","id":1115389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115381#post1115381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should not Predator Kings not jive with that on basista their Tribal Ban stoping them from entering city or using things in it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because every Predator King faithfully adheres to his tribal ban &amp; oath. No, really. Wait, there's a whole section in the Pure handbook about how a sizable population of them don't have the Harmony or care to give a damn about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:11:54-07:00","id":1115393,"title":"","content":"There's even a lodge devoted to eschewing it. They keep in touch by carrying something they made themselves, which means it's not of human craft. Making Penance is a big thing in the Predator Kings.<br /> <br /> The Pure, p100, 'Sarah Grey-Howler skips from corporation to corporation, leaving a trail of hidden fraud dealings behind her and racking up influential contacts in many companies just as she builds up huge savings scattered across several bank accounts. She tries her best to make her own clothes, but her initial good intentions waned and now she breaks her tribal ban every morning as she dresses and drives to work in her BMW. Her one attempt to stave off penance as long as she can is her pale leather jacket, made from the skin of a would-be rapist in the city park. She regrets that her position draws her away from Dire Wolf\u2019s favor and that she must struggle to maintain Harmony, but she believes the advantages of such a lifestyle outweigh the negative aspects. Every year, she tells herself that it\u2019ll be just one more year before she goes into the wilds for good, but the vow is half-hearted and always ignored, if never quite forgotten.'<br /> <br /> There's also more urban monsters, living like homeless thus not receiving shelter made by humans. And of course if you have wolf-blooded and werewolves with Crafts you could probably get a nice house built.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  My kid keeps saying of course so now I keep saying it 07-13-2017, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T18:12:13-07:00","id":1115743,"title":"","content":"So i am running Hunting Grounds: The Rockies, which has a Pack of Storm lord posers name Black Moon Extreme who hunt vampires because.....XP? The PC pack joined them in a hunt and one of them, the Ithaeur, fought a vampire (Daeva). The situation was simple and went as White Room scenario as it can get so i will share my experience with Vamp Vs Werewolf.<br /> <br /> If one has read the intro to the Rockies it more or less the initial scenario presented there with Black Moon Extreme crashing the car with the Daeva inside, difference here was that there was no trap just 3 ghouls with machine guns and the Daeva.<br /> <br /> Black Moon Extreme and the rest of the PC pack were dealing with the Ghouls while the Ithaeur went ahead and face the Daeva who just was getting out of the wreckage of the car. It was desert street at night.<br /> <br /> Ithaeur: Freshly change Ithaeur who was a biology teacher so she had Brawl 0, defense 4 and only her lunar gift at 1.<br /> <br /> Daeva: Club goer/socialite. To give her a chance, she had brawl 1. But aside from that she had defense 5 (Dex 3, Wits 3 and Athletics 2) but here is where system/Setting wise things start getting interesting because Werewolves has to ALWAYS justify their gifts (except lunar), they cant just spend their XP and get gifts. They have to RP finding a spirit to teach them and even getting the properly renown if they lack it.<br /> <br /> Not such things with Vampires, a Neonate can boost her core disciplines up to five with the XP she gets and nothing in the setting stops her. So this Daeva had the following disciplines: Potence 2, Celerity 4 (3 dots from disciplines in chargen + 3 more as she was &quot;Rising Star&quot; levels of XP (10) same as the Werewolf).<br /> <br /> So then there is the issue of the Predator jaws. Vampires are stupid durable that ALL damage (no counting banes) is Bashing, to kill a Vampire through conventional means you have to hit overflow twice so a regular vampire (lets assume Stamina 2) would have 21 health boxes before dead (7 + 7 + 7). Not so much with Predator jaws which inflict vampires with lethal so that reduces the amount of damage to 14 (7 + 7).<br /> <br /> Primal Fear is another issue, in Gauru Werewolf strips opponents of their defense. So thats a BIG plus on 1 on 1 combat, however the wording of it seems poorly written and what the intent/correct application of it is vague. It seems to imply to affect humans setting wise but seems to affect everyone. The idea of two gauru in the stripping each other of their defense because they both fear each other seems stupid. And an argument is to be made whether it would apply to vampire. But at the moment i made a ruling that it applied to the current situation.<br /> <br /> So this was a fight between 2 Supernatural not made for combat in which the whole fight was carried over by their supernatural powers. Not going to go into turn-by-turn because that was months ago and it would take too long but the main highlights of the fight were:<ul><li>Contrary to what other has said a fight between a Werewolf and a Vampire is slow. The quantity of overflow nescesary to kill a vampire make it so.</li> <li>The time limit of the Gauru form is a non issue in 1 on 1 but the extra regeneration makes Vigor a must for a vampire. The very lucky hits that reached overflow from the vampire to the werewolf were because of the extra dices and damage that potence gave. And while the regeneration does wipe aways all lethal damage once you reach overflow each turn it becomes easier.</li> <li>Celerity is useless for Vampires unless one houserule that primal fear doesn't work on vampire or that only the defense given by celerity counts. The lack of defense makes.</li> </ul><br /> In conclusion Vampire vs Werewolf has a pretty interesting synergy to it between Predator jaws and the way Vampires process damage in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-13-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T03:16:16-07:00","id":1115860,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> Couple of things:<br /> <br /> 7 Lethal from jaws damage would have created a torpid vampire, at which point their destruction is trivial. <br /> <br /> Primal Fear doesn't completely depletes defense: just the skill part of the equation, nevermind Celerity does adds to defense. So the vampire's defense would be a whooping 3 + 4 equating 7. Regarding how to portray it, I just mention that Gauru is just THAT faster than even the bullet dodging hybrid forms of Dalu and Urshul.<br /> <br /> Note also, that at Celerity 4, escaping with unholy speed in an empty street would have been trivial as well. Why exactly did the vampire fight to her death? Frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T04:25:29-07:00","id":1115872,"title":"","content":"Or since it's called Primal Fear, maybe rather than just fast, it's more like the sight of a 3 meters tall 600 kg hulking creature of muscle, claws, teeth and fur charging at you and towering over you strips an intelligent creature of all they had learned and they react on pure instinct alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T04:48:41-07:00","id":1115883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115860#post1115860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple of things:<br /> Primal Fear doesn't completely depletes defense: just the skill part of the equation, nevermind Celerity does adds to defense. So the vampire's defense would be a whooping 3 + 4 equating 7. </div> </div> </div> </div>You are right i miss-wrote that rule in my notes. It should have been a battle of chance dies then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115860#post1115860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7 Lethal from jaws damage would have created a torpid vampire, at which point their destruction is trivial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also right, i skimmed on the vampire rules and i miss that one. However i do think is a bad rule and i would remove it for future Vamp Vs Werewolves fights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115860#post1115860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note also, that at Celerity 4, escaping with unholy speed in an empty street would have been trivial as well. Why exactly did the vampire fight to her death? Frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>IC was because of frenzy and it was either fight the lone ithaeur of climb a flaming wreck of a limo. OOC was because if the vampire had fled there would have been no game, in that particular instance the Ithaeur joined Black Moon Extreme\u00b4s hunt against the wish of the rest of the PC pack, and said PC pack was racing through trying to extract her before she did something stupid. Had the vampire fled the nothing would have happened, maybe Black Moon Extreme would have chased the vampire but the PC pack would remove the Ithaeur by literary grabbing her by the back of her neck like a puppy and put her on the corner. There was no room for even the vampire to know who the Ithaeur because she change form to Urshul before the Daeva exited the vehicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115872#post1115872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or since it's called Primal Fear, maybe rather than just fast, it's more like the sight of a 3 meters tall 600 kg hulking creature of muscle, claws, teeth and fur charging at you and towering over you strips an intelligent creature of all they had learned and they react on pure instinct alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that against other Werewolf in Gauru form it doesnt follow. &quot;Oh no! He is a 3 meters tall 600 kg hulking creature of muscle, claws, teeth and fur.....just like me! and i kinda see that everyday so shouldnt be surprised at this point!&quot;<br /> <br /> And an argument is to be made if a Vampire who has fought an Gangrel riding the wave with aggravated claws is not more scarier.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115860#post1115860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;2179&quot;]Regarding how to portray it, I just mention that Gauru is just THAT faster than even the bullet dodging hybrid forms of Dalu and Urshul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that doesn't follow why it does remove athletics from other Werewolves. If both are in Gauru then they both shouldn't strips each others athletics from their defense. Also if it was thing of speed then Celerity should do the trick too. Its just a bad written rule, wording only making sense when used against humans and probably there just to balance the short time of the gauru form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-14-2017, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:13:13-07:00","id":1115889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115883#post1115883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that against other Werewolf in Gauru form it doesnt follow. &quot;Oh no! He is a 3 meters tall 600 kg hulking creature of muscle, claws, teeth and fur.....just like me! and i kinda see that everyday so shouldnt be surprised at this point!&quot;<br /> <br /> And an argument is to be made if a Vampire who has fought an Gangrel riding the wave with aggravated claws is not more scarier.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about what's scarier now. It's called Primal Fear, it's a fear that's been bred into people since before they started building things called homes and deciding a long piece of wood could be used for something. Vampires aren't afraid of the dark, usually. They are afraid of the Final Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that doesn't follow why it does remove athletics from other Werewolves. If both are in Gauru then they both shouldn't strips each others athletics from their defense. Also if it was thing of speed then Celerity should do the trick too. Its just a bad written rule, wording only making sense when used against humans and probably there just to balance the short time of the gauru form. </div> </div> </div>And even in gauru there's a human part of you that feels the same. When Kuruth occurs, though, werewolves don't target one another when raging, so even a Predator King and Iron Master will start hunting together.<br /> <br /> It's only badly written in that there's no separate paragraph explaining that the Defense loss part isn't just for 'lesser enemies.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:15:14-07:00","id":1115890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Or since it's called Primal Fear, maybe rather than just fast, it's more like the sight of a 3 meters tall 600 kg hulking creature of muscle, claws, teeth and fur charging at you and towering over you strips an intelligent creature of all they had learned and they react on pure instinct alone.</span><br /> </span><br /> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> </span><br /> <br /> Which is kind of odd, when you get right down to it. Those kinds of movements end up being shoved into your hind brain, not your frontal lobe. Dodging is instinctual. But this and that is a separate matter; the exact mechanics can be reflavored in any number of ways, including as a function of long reach, or a trick of Lunacy messing with the victim's perceptions and mind to dull their reactions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:17:21-07:00","id":1115892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115883#post1115883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> OOC was because if the vampire had fled there would have been no game,</div> </div> </div> </div> In short, the vampire was given the idiot ball for the sake of being able to kill them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:18:59-07:00","id":1115893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115889#post1115889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about what's scarier now. It's called Primal Fear, it's a fear that's been bred into people since before they started building things called homes and deciding a long piece of wood could be used for something. Vampires aren't afraid of the dark, usually. They are afraid of the Final Death.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind i mentioned Primal Fear in relation to Gauru vs Gauru, not Gauru in kuruth vs Gauru in Kuruth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115889#post1115889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only badly written in that there's no separate paragraph explaining that the Defense loss part isn't just for 'lesser enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ymmv to me is badly written because is not just for lesser enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:22:59-07:00","id":1115894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115892#post1115892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In short, the vampire was given the idiot ball for the sake of being able to kill them?</div> </div> </div> </div>OCC? Sure, pretty much. IC? Maybe the vampire in frenzy would have being able to jump over the pilling flaming wreck of a limo, maybe not. I would say that between 1 scrawny (Stamina 1) looking Gauru or fire the vampire would have chosen the scrawny looking Gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:23:01-07:00","id":1115895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115893#post1115893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind i mentioned Primal Fear in relation to Gauru vs Gauru, not Gauru in kuruth vs Gauru in Kuruth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. I just made a point of clarifying that all werewolf battles do not come down to gauru vs gauru.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ymmv to me is badly written because is not just for lesser enemies. </div> </div> </div>It would probably be more accurate to say you don't like it. Badly written implies there's some problem with the text, and based on people's confusion for how it works, I can understand that, but that's apparently not what you mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115894#post1115894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that between 1 scrawny (Stamina 1) looking Gauru or fire the vampire would have chosen the scrawny looking Gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gauru adds 2 Stamina, at least, and 2 Size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-14-2017, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:25:11-07:00","id":1115896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115895#post1115895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would probably be more accurate to say you don't like it. Badly written implies there's some problem with the text, and based on people's confusion for how it works, I can understand that, but that's apparently not what you mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, the fluff seems to indicate is for lesser enemies while the actual mechanics are for all enemies. To me is badly written because the mechanics dont reflect the fluff. Your take is that is badly written because the fluff doesnt reflect the mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:26:24-07:00","id":1115897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115895#post1115895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gauru adds 2 Stamina, at least, and 2 Size.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant her human stats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:24:27-07:00","id":1115916,"title":"","content":"Lesser enemies use down and dirty combat. Just losing the skill part of your defence means you're a threat. <br /> <br /> You could fluff it as innate fighting instincts compensating for the opponents ability to avoid harm if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T11:26:01-07:00","id":1116031,"title":"","content":"I always just though Primal Fear was less an effect you had on people... and more that YOU were a Primal Fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T05:42:37-07:00","id":1116334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1115892#post1115892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In short, the vampire was given the idiot ball for the sake of being able to kill them?</div> </div> </div> </div>[Agreeing]Also it is not true that the vampire fleeing would have meant no game, there is the whole &quot; What just happened?&quot; scene, the follow up investigating scene, possible find the vampire scene, which then makes a social or combat scene. All of which is more interesting in my opinion than &quot;it died like a mindless video game AI bot&quot; scene. Let's not forget the escaping vampire likely snitched about the incident to coterie, Elysium court or Covenant friends, thus alerting the whole vampire cacophony to a mad pack of bone gnawing hoodlums. <br /> &quot;White room&quot; is never a good thing in the game, &quot;White room&quot; means without intelligently thought out context from the setting and characters, and hopefully you always have intelligently thought out context from the setting and characters in the game. [/Agreeing]<br /> <br /> Because in a real game intelligently thought out context from the setting and characters are going to likely tip the scales of conflicts in either direction, we can more trends for certain types of conflict but the overall topic is interestingly moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-15-2017, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T06:09:20-07:00","id":1116343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1116334#post1116334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there is the whole &quot; What just happened?&quot; scene, the follow up investigating scene, possible find the vampire scene, which then makes a social or combat scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not it wouldnt, the rest of the PC party wanted to extract the Ithaeur ASAP and not hunt a vampire. The ithaeur wanted to kill vampire because fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1116334#post1116334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget the escaping vampire likely snitched about the incident to coterie, Elysium court or Covenant friends, thus alerting the whole vampire cacophony to a mad pack of bone gnawing hoodlums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also wrong. The setting as presented (Hunting grounds: The rockies) had NPC pack Black Moon Extreme killing various vampire and thus Vampire society already alerted. Had the vampire flee, the rest of the PC pack would grab the Ithaeur by the back of the neck, drag him away and forbid her from talking to BMX because they are a bad influence for everything. The vampire hunt would have been abandoned (as only the Ithaeur and BMX did the rite) and as the PC pack were all in furry forms, no way to track it back to them. They would force the Ithaeur to remove himself and them from that particular plot, which the ithaeur would have done because her player is a pushover and that moment when she disobey the pack and did something &quot;bad&quot; would have had absolutely no weight or consequence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1116334#post1116334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;White room&quot; is never a good thing in the game, &quot;White room&quot; means without intelligently thought out context from the setting and characters, and hopefully you always have intelligently thought out context from the setting and characters in the game. [/Agreeing]<br /> <br /> Because in a real game intelligently thought out context from the setting and characters are going to likely tip the scales of conflicts in either direction, we can more trends for certain types of conflict but the overall topic is interestingly moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, white room has a time and place. Some people disregard it but it is a nice way to test 1 on 1 combat mechanics. And some people assume that NPC always must act with the most absolute logic when in reality people act dumb and in games PC act dumb too.<br /> <br /> Normally their course of action wasnt the best course possible course of action possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-15-2017, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T08:29:30-07:00","id":1116398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1116343#post1116343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not it wouldnt, the rest of the PC party wanted to extract the Ithaeur ASAP and not hunt a vampire. The ithaeur wanted to kill vampire because fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also wrong. The setting as presented (Hunting grounds: The rockies) had NPC pack Black Moon Extreme killing various vampire and thus Vampire society already alerted. Had the vampire flee, the rest of the PC pack would grab the Ithaeur by the back of the neck, drag him away and forbid her from talking to BMX because they are a bad influence for everything. The vampire hunt would have been abandoned (as only the Ithaeur and BMX did the rite) and as the PC pack were all in furry forms, no way to track it back to them. They would force the Ithaeur to remove himself and them from that particular plot, which the ithaeur would have done because her player is a pushover and that moment when she disobey the pack and did something &quot;bad&quot; would have had absolutely no weight or consequence. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree, white room has a time and place. Some people disregard it but it is a nice way to test 1 on 1 combat mechanics. And some people assume that NPC always must act with the most absolute logic when in reality people act dumb and in games PC act dumb too.<br /> <br /> Normally their course of action wasnt the best course possible course of action possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree white room has a place, like theoretical physic, which is to say not in actual application. Useful for system design right before play testing starts to try how it works with context. <br /> <br /> About the specific chronicle I think a specific description and update on last know location of the vampire hunting werewolf pack would still be meaningful to how the game could play out. Or is the entire vampire template given the stupid ball so they are basically clusters of stats without intelligence or motivations, and just objects to be killed? Fighting of course is an option, but really attempts at negotation via proxies and bribes/holding leveage against non-uratha pack members (or how the vampires would see it as striking ar mortal pawns, a favorite kindred hobby in the danse macabre) or alternatively vanishing via leaving the area, hiding behind moral proxies that bring food to them, and hiding via Torpor are much more reasonable reactions that wading into combat. Also please do consider we are discussing a 1st edition setting in 2nd edition context and that more than justified a reexamination and ST rewriting it a bit to update it to fit current themes. A setting is a stage, what the actors do on the stage should reflect character motivation, and if it isn't dying a martyr or suicide then a good chunk of that motivation should be to stay alive, which rings true of real life motivation.<br /> <br /> If the PCs were not in fact hunting vampires, then you have a situation where it'll be assumed they crashed the vehicle in order to hunt that vampire, and they'd be identified with that tactic and intent (sounds like it was ST created forced plot point to create drama, thus not intentional for the PCs) then a dark comedy of errors ensues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-15-2017, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T08:41:04-07:00","id":1116405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1116343#post1116343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, white room has a time and place. Some people disregard it but it is a nice way to test 1 on 1 combat mechanics. And some people assume that NPC always must act with the most absolute logic when in reality people act dumb and in games PC act dumb too.<br /> <br /> Normally their course of action wasnt the best course possible course of action possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if the vamp was in frenzy is completely natural that the Beast wanted to fucking murder the werewolf that screwed it's limo sideways. YMMV.<br /> <br /> That being said, if the vamp had escaped I would have gotten it to hunt the Ithaeur (and/or his/her loved ones) and therefore the pack for the audacity. Thus bringing the pack into the plot. But, y'know, hindsight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T10:04:58-07:00","id":1116451,"title":"","content":"Guys come on, not everyone's going to run their game the same way or come up with the same results. Loki was posting a snippet of their game, not asking for help dealing with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T22:04:32-07:00","id":1116724,"title":"","content":"A vampire is very effective in fighting a werewolf; all the vampire has to do is wait for the werewolf to die of old-age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T13:19:09-07:00","id":1116959,"title":"","content":"It's actually a bit vague whether or not they do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T14:04:33-07:00","id":1116971,"title":"","content":"I confess that I'm a bit surprised no one's mentioned Claws of the Unholy yet. ^^ If you want a vampire who can go toe-to-toe with Gauru-form, you could do worse than a Gangrel Sworn of the Axe; it's not exactly XP-cheap, but Protean 4 + decent Blood Potency + Coil of the Beast 4 makes for an undead Wolverine, even before adding any physical Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Even granting that social-fu is the more default archetype of VtR characters, though, there's another dimension to this that I think is going under-mentioned: the market price of silver. Having mortal resources, even if they're tied up in property or favors or networks of blood dolls, means at least some opportunity to translate those resources into cash... and cash translates into precious metal, if you've got enough of it. <br /> <br /> If the city's Damned really feel their unlives are at stake, you can imagine the call going out: &quot;We. Need. Silver. Name your price.&quot; Two weeks later, their cash reserves are depleted and they're under favor debts to foreign Princes that will take half a century to pay off... but every vampire and ghoul is packing fully-automatic weapons and enough silver bullets to supply an infantry squad. (If the Prince is feeling *really* extravagant [or paranoid], s/he might even commission silver armor for the city's high-and-mighty; you can bite us, puppies, but you won't enjoy it very much.) Yes, the wolves move fast, and those Defense scores can be quite decent, but autofire and multiple attackers can compensate. Suddenly Iron Masters and any other wolves with Shaping/Technology gifts are in high demand, the better to sabotage the leeches' new toys (which of course means they're priority targets if the vampires find out who they are...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T16:14:02-07:00","id":1116999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1116971#post1116971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I confess that I'm a bit surprised no one's mentioned Claws of the Unholy yet. ^^ If you want a vampire who can go toe-to-toe with Gauru-form, you could do worse than a Gangrel Sworn of the Axe; it's not exactly XP-cheap, but Protean 4 + decent Blood Potency + Coil of the Beast 4 makes for an undead Wolverine, even before adding any physical Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're dealing more with generalities, which is why people haven't brought things like that up or werewolves with gifts that let them breathe fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even granting that social-fu is the more default archetype of VtR characters, though, there's another dimension to this that I think is going under-mentioned: the market price of silver. Having mortal resources, even if they're tied up in property or favors or networks of blood dolls, means at least some opportunity to translate those resources into cash... and cash translates into precious metal, if you've got enough of it. </div> </div> </div>And Iguazu seemed to be talking more about individual fights, rather than some kind of war where one side waits for the other to kill them.<br /> <br /> Have you had any personal experiences with werewolves and vampires fighting one another in a game you played?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-16-2017, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T16:15:45-07:00","id":1117000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1116971#post1116971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I confess that I'm a bit surprised no one's mentioned Claws of the Unholy yet. ^^ If you want a vampire who can go toe-to-toe with Gauru-form, you could do worse than a Gangrel Sworn of the Axe; it's not exactly XP-cheap, but Protean 4 + decent Blood Potency + Coil of the Beast 4 makes for an undead Wolverine, even before adding any physical Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Even granting that social-fu is the more default archetype of VtR characters, though, there's another dimension to this that I think is going under-mentioned: the market price of silver. Having mortal resources, even if they're tied up in property or favors or networks of blood dolls, means at least some opportunity to translate those resources into cash... and cash translates into precious metal, if you've got enough of it.<br /> <br /> If the city's Damned really feel their unlives are at stake, you can imagine the call going out: &quot;We. Need. Silver. Name your price.&quot; Two weeks later, their cash reserves are depleted and they're under favor debts to foreign Princes that will take half a century to pay off... but every vampire and ghoul is packing fully-automatic weapons and enough silver bullets to supply an infantry squad. (If the Prince is feeling *really* extravagant [or paranoid], s/he might even commission silver armor for the city's high-and-mighty; you can bite us, puppies, but you won't enjoy it very much.) Yes, the wolves move fast, and those Defense scores can be quite decent, but autofire and multiple attackers can compensate. Suddenly Iron Masters and any other wolves with Shaping/Technology gifts are in high demand, the better to sabotage the leeches' new toys (which of course means they're priority targets if the vampires find out who they are...)</div> </div> </div> </div>By this same logic, any pack with any lick of sense will invest in fire weaponry... which is going to be loads cheaper than whatever the vampires can get for silver and doesn't have the tradeoff that it makes for poor weaponry. This is to say nothing about all of the pyromania causing effects that are basically a dime a dozen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and the silver armor is kinda... useless. It's not going to stop anything and is terrible for armor because it's a soft, precious metal that's way heavier than iron, with arguably no benefit. In fact, I'd argue the silver armor will be a terrible flop worse than the original Hulk Buster and get the owner killed so hard that it gets mocked for years down the line... (possibly because a rival sold the idea to him in the first place).<br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously, it's safer not to go down the rabbit hole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 07-16-2017, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T16:19:20-07:00","id":1117001,"title":"","content":"Silver armour wouldn't do shit. That's not how their weakness works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T17:09:40-07:00","id":1117013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117001#post1117001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver armour wouldn't do shit. That's not how their weakness works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, Pure at least can't abide the touch of silver, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T17:31:59-07:00","id":1117018,"title":"","content":"I agree with most of the above posters. Werewolf vs Vampire combat is something to be avoided by most vampires...it just doesn't usually work out well for them. Especially since there are some really nice werewolf Gifts and Merits that only enhance a werewolf pack's fighting abilities when attacking as a pack. A werewolf's strength is not in himself, but in his pack.<br /> <br /> In general, however, a werewolf pack's only real reason to aggress against vampires is when said vampire is screwing around in the werewolf pack's territory. Again, this doesn't usually end well for a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13210-fossmano1","name":"FossMaNo1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T17:51:39-07:00","id":1117022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117013#post1117013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, Pure at least can't abide the touch of silver, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We're talking at most giving them a rash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T17:57:36-07:00","id":1117024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117000#post1117000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By this same logic, any pack with any lick of sense will invest in fire weaponry... which is going to be loads cheaper than whatever the vampires can get for silver and doesn't have the tradeoff that it makes for poor weaponry. This is to say nothing about all of the pyromania causing effects that are basically a dime a dozen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple points here. Yes, investing in fire is a great countermeasure for vampire hunters, mortal and otherwise... but while sources of fire are cheaper and easier to find than sources of silver, I think you're conflating ease of acquisition with capacity to be weaponized. Fire is difficult to project at any kind of distance, esp. for mortals &amp; Wolf-Blooded without overt supernatural powers, without a) attracting a lot of attention, b) endangering yourself and the people/buildings around you, and c) attracting even more attention by virtue of being unusually bulky, assuming some sort of flamethrower setup.<br /> <br /> By contrast, silver bullets or small blades are easily concealed, attract no more attention than a gun or knife otherwise would, can be operated by Joe Mortal, and (with a decent rifle &amp; scope) can reach out and touch wolves from a long ways away.<br /> <br /> As for silver armor: here, too, I think you're leaping to a conclusion too quickly. Yes, silver is softer &amp; weaker, and a point's worth off the armor or weapon rating is entirely warranted to reflect that. But it's still worked metal; if silver bullets &amp; silver blades hold their shape well enough to do the job when subjected to the stresses of a gun barrel or a stabbing, silver armor is strong enough to offer some limited utility. And from WtF 2nd, pg. 101: &quot;A non-damaging touch with silver doesn't cause damage, but causes intense pain so long as the werewolf remains in contact, and leaves lasting scars as if from aggravated wounds.&quot; I'd suggest the Agony Tilt could reflect what happens to a werewolf who tries to take a bite out of a silver-armored opponent; it *hurts,* and makes it that much easier for said opponent to exploit an opening.<br /> <br /> RE: GMing - not yet! Most of my GMing experience has been with Pathfinder; in CoD I've done a mortals game and a Vamp game several years ago.<br /> <br /> Edit: as for &quot;down the rabbit hole&quot; - if you mean &quot;find some capital-A Answer as to 'who wins the battle of the splats?&quot; then I couldn't agree more, and that's not what I'm going for. (I'm a Mage fan anyway, I have no dog in this fight! XD ) But the question &quot;if your story slowly built up to a city-wide conflict between its Xs and its Ys, how would that play out, and what could each side bring to the table?&quot; is an interesting one, if explored thoughtfully and with room for compelling character choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","user":"AmusedByIrony","date":". 07-16-2017, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T18:11:30-07:00","id":1117026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117024#post1117024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple points here. Yes, investing in fire is a great countermeasure for vampire hunters, mortal and otherwise... but while sources of fire are cheaper and easier to find than sources of silver, I think you're conflating ease of acquisition with capacity to be weaponized. Fire is difficult to project at any kind of distance, esp. for mortals &amp; Wolf-Blooded without overt supernatural powers, without a) attracting a lot of attention, b) endangering yourself and the people/buildings around you, and c) attracting even more attention by virtue of being unusually bulky, assuming some sort of flamethrower setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Werewolf Gift Tongue of Flame allows you to create and control fire that's as easy to get as Protean 4. If you want to go further, a werewolf with Tongue of Flame and Catastrophe can drown a 20 mile area in fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By contrast, silver bullets or small blades are easily concealed, attract no more attention than a gun or knife otherwise would, can be operated by Joe Mortal, and (with a decent rifle &amp; scope) can reach out and touch wolves from a long ways away. </div> </div> </div>Unless taken by surprise, in most forms werewolves have full Defense against Firearms. For that matter, since we're white rooming now, werewolves can just walk through the Shadow to a vampire's den, pop across with help from their totem or Moon Gift in the middle of the day, and saw their heads off one by one without ever having to deal with a ghoul or other guardian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-16-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T18:33:23-07:00","id":1117031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117026#post1117026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Werewolf Gift Tongue of Flame allows you to create and control fire that's as easy to get as Protean 4. If you want to go further, a werewolf with Tongue of Flame and Catastrophe can drown a 20 mile area in fire.<br /> <br /> Unless taken by surprise, in most forms werewolves have full Defense against Firearms. For that matter, since we're white rooming now, werewolves can just walk through the Shadow to a vampire's den, pop across with help from their totem or Moon Gift in the middle of the day, and saw their heads off one by one without ever having to deal with a ghoul or other guardian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and those wolves would become both prime assets and prime targets. But Catastrophe begs the question: if your shaman is willing to firebomb a 20-mile radius, why shouldn't every faction in the city unite to take you down? Theoretical capacity for destruction doesn't translate into applied force if you can't apply it precisely enough to make the political fallout worth the price.<br /> <br /> And yes, Defense vs. firearms is a major advantage for the wolves. Tactic: lure them into enfilade and smother them with bullets, counting on weight of numbers; making new ghouls is cheaper and quicker than waiting for new Wolf-Blooded or Uratha to change and replenish the ranks. Counter-tactic: Shadow-side ambushes &amp; daytime assaults, just as you suggest (or, alternatively, emulating a wolfpack and slowly nipping at the flanks of the Prince's criminal contacts, drying up a supply line here, attacking a shipment there, trying to draw the vamps out and pick them off a few at a time...) <br /> <br /> *Counter*-counter-tactic: let the Circle or the Ordo devise a ritual to speak with the spirits of blood and fear and pain that follow vampires like smoke, and ask their price for standing guard on the Shadow-side...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T18:37:40-07:00","id":1117034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1116971#post1116971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I confess that I'm a bit surprised no one's mentioned Claws of the Unholy yet. ^^ If you want a vampire who can go toe-to-toe with Gauru-form, you could do worse than a Gangrel Sworn of the Axe; it's not exactly XP-cheap, but Protean 4 + decent Blood Potency + Coil of the Beast 4 makes for an undead Wolverine, even before adding any physical Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. If you want to do a good Gangrel shredder, forget the Coil. Go with protean claws and swarm form. That makes you pretty much immune to every kind of damage, save for an AoE Elemental gift, and you're dealing aggravated damage to pretty much an entire pack at once.<br /> <br /> To put it simply, no one is bringing up most of a vampire's abilities, because that's just going to become a &quot;whatever you can do, I can do better!&quot; type situation, and that's just going to be silly. The real problem is racial bais. Well, game bias with supernatural races. Far too often, if you favor one race over another, then clearly, that race gets a multitude of advantages while the other tends to end up being strictly limited unnecessarily. Critical parts of one race or another gets downplayed to uselessness, while minor parts of the other get upplayed to trump card status. Happens all the time in these discussions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-16-2017, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T18:47:31-07:00","id":1117036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117031#post1117031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, and those wolves would become both prime assets and prime targets. But Catastrophe begs the question: if your shaman is willing to firebomb a 20-mile radius, why shouldn't every faction in the city unite to take you down? Theoretical capacity for destruction doesn't translate into applied force if you can't apply it precisely enough to make the political fallout worth the price.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like the men wearing silver armor as they march around the city with their guns? Even in Texas that would raise eyebrows and have police arresting ghouls. And with Catastrophe it's just up to a 20 mile area, you can do it considerably smaller, like just dropping it on an Elysium. Though at that point you could just do it with Tongue of Flame.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, Defense vs. firearms is a major advantage for the wolves. Tactic: lure them into enfilade and smother them with bullets, counting on weight of numbers; making new ghouls is cheaper and quicker than waiting for new Wolf-Blooded or Uratha to change and replenish the ranks. Counter-tactic: Shadow-side ambushes &amp; daytime assaults, just as you suggest (or, alternatively, emulating a wolfpack and slowly nipping at the flanks of the Prince's criminal contacts, drying up a supply line here, attacking a shipment there, trying to draw the vamps out and pick them off a few at a time...) </div> </div> </div>Making new ghouls is easy, making them useful isn't. But why would the werewolves in your scenarios walk into traps when they have so many abilities that allow them to sense things like traps, ghouls, and vampires?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Counter*-counter-tactic: let the Circle or the Ordo devise a ritual to speak with the spirits of blood and fear and pain that follow vampires like smoke, and ask their price for standing guard on the Shadow-side... </div> </div> </div>I think the Circle would have a better chance with that, but I don't think pain or fear spirits would really follow vampires around. Maybe fear from some with Nightmare but vampires don't generally feel pain themselves and their bite is painless and even pleasurable most of the time. Death spirits, maybe, or just vampire and leech spirits. Though of course taking down things isn't limited to humans and vampires and it's basically part of the werewolf lifestyle, spirits are not an exception.<br /> <br /> Not counting niche things like the Eaters of the Dead or Lodge of the Willow Branch whose lives revolve around destroying vampires, if you're dealing with an entire domain of vampires causing you trouble, it's appropriate that the Ivory Claws would have the best way to deal with them. Their sacred hunt allows for them to sense those who have familial and communal bonds with their sacred prey. Any attempt to block or hinder a werewolf, or refuse to provide information, is penalized by the werewolf's Primal Urge. Using this a hunt led by an Ivory Claw would be able to easily suss out vampiric connections, shut them down and isolate them. Then let the werewolf side do their thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T18:57:49-07:00","id":1117038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117034#post1117034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. If you want to do a good Gangrel shredder, forget the Coil. Go with protean claws and swarm form. That makes you pretty much immune to every kind of damage, save for an AoE Elemental gift, and you're dealing aggravated damage to pretty much an entire pack at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, I can see where you're coming from RE: Swarm Form. RAI, I think I'd bar that combination in any game I run. For a Watsonian justification: unleashing the Claws needs a degree of mass and muscle behind them that tiny bats just can't muster. On the Doylist side: all-purpose aggravated damage to multiple targets at once is just too potent to hand out without some kind of resource cost. (Mages can do it, but only with a Reach for Advanced Scale and Mana.) Maybe dial it back to X Vitae for every turn the vampire wants to use the Claws while in Swarm Form, reflecting the additional unholy power s/he's bleeding into all those gnashing, flying jaws...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T19:05:12-07:00","id":1117039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117031#post1117031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, and those wolves would become both prime assets and prime targets. But Catastrophe begs the question: if your shaman is willing to firebomb a 20-mile radius, why shouldn't every faction in the city unite to take you down? Theoretical capacity for destruction doesn't translate into applied force if you can't apply it precisely enough to make the political fallout worth the price...</div> </div> </div> </div>Very valid point. <br /> <br /> Fire bombing a 20 mile radius which is a major metropolitan area not already subject to carpet bombing is a great way to get a Time Master or Archmage any of the Seer of the Throne/Pentacle/Free Council that would likely not be too keen on allowing a breach of the various supernatural conspiracies that grievous. Not mentioning Demon, Angel, or God machine shenanigans to undo stuff like that too.<br /> <br /> Also besides editing after the fact you have to keep in mind prophetic power that would get a tip off long before something that including Knowing Practice of Fate or Time Arcanums, the Omen Numina and Cahalith Prophetic Dreams?<br /> <br /> While having to ST dozens if not s couple hundred of beings which would foresee the event and then intervene is challenging but would be accurate. How many other Uratha packs would try to stop you based off the idea &quot;The herd must not know&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-16-2017, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T19:22:54-07:00","id":1117045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117034#post1117034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. If you want to do a good Gangrel shredder, forget the Coil. Go with protean claws and swarm form. That makes you pretty much immune to every kind of damage, save for an AoE Elemental gift, and you're dealing aggravated damage to pretty much an entire pack at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just take less damage in Swarm Form, damage is reduced to 1, or 2 on an Exceptional Success. And you use the Strength and Brawl of the creature you've made, which in a size 0 or 1 creature is going to be small. Bats have a dicepool of 2, Rats have 1.<br /> <br /> Swarm Form is better for harassment or utilitarian use than combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T22:08:41-07:00","id":1117097,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13570\" data-vbnamecard=\"13570\">AmusedByIrony</a>:<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I can see Werewolves under such circumstances recruiting boons from Helions, suddenly silver doesn't helps that much if being in the presence of a pack causes aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> In my game I didn't even needed to get the Elemental gift, just bound fire elementals into grenades for Catastrophe effects, wiped out 90% of the borough's Circle of the Crone as they had their revelries, without even rolling Initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T23:05:01-07:00","id":1117103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117097#post1117097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13570\" data-vbnamecard=\"13570\">AmusedByIrony</a>:<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I can see Werewolves under such circumstances recruiting boons from Helions, suddenly silver doesn't helps that much if being in the presence of a pack causes aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> In my game I didn't even needed to get the Elemental gift, just bound fire elementals into grenades for Catastrophe effects, wiped out 90% of the borough's Circle of the Crone as they had their revelries, without even rolling Initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sunlight doesn't automatically deal aggravated damage to vampires. It depends on their humanity, and depending on their blood potency it might not even physically harm them for the duration of the combat. It'd probably make them flee or piss them off though.<br /> <br /> Also the fire spirits thing is a pretty neat idea; were there any other covenants in the territory that reacted to that, or was it just circle of the Crone vampires?<br /> <br /> But yeah, measuring werewolves versus vampires based off of supernatural prowess doesn't really end in the vampire's favor; in general they don't have any access to otherworldy realms like werewolves (there is an Abyss like realm that some cruac users have access to, but it doesn't really get much coverage, and neither does the strix realm, but that is admittedly very hard to get to.)<br /> <br /> Werewolf rites are also capable of effecting large stretches of land, while vampire powers can't do so.<br /> <br /> Oh, and if there is a powerful voivode in the territory then there's a chance that they can grant every vampire in the domain the ability to smother supernatural fire via a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T07:02:53-07:00","id":1117180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117045#post1117045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You just take less damage in Swarm Form, damage is reduced to 1, or 2 on an Exceptional Success. And you use the Strength and Brawl of the creature you've made, which in a size 0 or 1 creature is going to be small. Bats have a dicepool of 2, Rats have 1.<br /> <br /> Swarm Form is better for harassment or utilitarian use than combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's only one way of reading it. I always took you use the base vampire's own dicepool when in swarm form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T07:37:17-07:00","id":1117185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117180#post1117180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's only one way of reading it. I always took you use the base vampire's own dicepool when in swarm form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swarm Form requires you to take Beast's Skin. 'When taking the Beast\u2019s Skin, some Gangrel can instead become a swarm of small creatures: Size 0 or Size 1 animals. The character may perceive through any of the senses of any individual creature in the swarm, but the swarm acts as a single entity.'<br /> <br /> Scroll down to Beast's Skin. 'In animal form, she takes on the beast\u2019s Physical Attributes and Skills, and its Size, Speed, and Health. She can move and sense and attack in any way that the animal can \u2014 a shark can swim and bite and sense blood, while a rat can scurry and bite, and a crow can fly. She may be unable to use some Physical Merits at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.' They can still use their Disciplines, though, so the other Protean changes would be available.<br /> <br /> The RAW seems pretty clear. Swarm Form doesn't offer any exception for using the vampire's Attributes and Skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T07:39:48-07:00","id":1117186,"title":"","content":"Fire spirits are both more reliable for damage and less hostile to werewolves than helions, so they're the obvious choice in spirit allies against a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:05:57-07:00","id":1117197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117185#post1117185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Swarm Form requires you to take Beast's Skin. 'When taking the Beast\u2019s Skin, some Gangrel can instead become a swarm of small creatures: Size 0 or Size 1 animals. The character may perceive through any of the senses of any individual creature in the swarm, but the swarm acts as a single entity.'<br /> <br /> Scroll down to Beast's Skin. 'In animal form, she takes on the beast\u2019s Physical Attributes and Skills, and its Size, Speed, and Health. She can move and sense and attack in any way that the animal can \u2014 a shark can swim and bite and sense blood, while a rat can scurry and bite, and a crow can fly. She may be unable to use some Physical Merits at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.' They can still use their Disciplines, though, so the other Protean changes would be available.<br /> <br /> The RAW seems pretty clear. Swarm Form doesn't offer any exception for using the vampire's Attributes and Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, but then again it's pretty dumb that when using any creature with a size of 0, and most size 1, you would have 0 Strength or Brawl. You would be using a chance die pretty much always. Seems too weak to me.<br /> <br /> I tried the Swarm Form with the Vampires stats in a game I ran and it wasn't that powerful actually. I tried a BP 3 Gangrel with Strength 4, Brawl 4 so I was rolling 11 dice with Willpower against one starting stats Werewolf that had only 1 Essence and no Gifts at all. Granted, I had horrible luck with the dice, but still only managed to force it to change to Gauru for 2 turn until all blood was spent and Health gone.<br /> <br /> I see why some have resorted to using the swarm mechanics (from Demon I believe), since Swarm Form is pretty unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:13:01-07:00","id":1117200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117197#post1117197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is true, but then again it's pretty dumb that when using any creature with a size of 0, and most size 1, you would have 0 Strength or Brawl. You would be using a chance die pretty much always. Seems too weak to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... Because when you're so small you're basically a mouse or a rat, your stength at normal size would hardly take into effect because of... well, mechanics. As in physics. Square cube law would basically render even super strong rodents... as just rodents because the gulf of difference between small creatures and humans is just that obscene. As a swarm there's only so much you can do, and you'd be worse at most strength based tasks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd say using something other than strength like the protean component as part of the damage modifier might be more applicable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:19:33-07:00","id":1117204,"title":"","content":"Also, different than Beast Skin: Whereas that uses the creatures speed, in Swarm Form &quot;The swarm moves at the vampire\u2019s Speed, modified for the creatures\u2019 Size, in any logical direction.&quot;<br /> And this passage would have no reason to exist if it was always 1 or chance die: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To attack those within her swarm, roll Strength + Brawl, ignoring Defense. Divide the damage however you wish among those inside. Apply a victim\u2019s armor to the damage normally. </div> </div> </div>Why even ignore Def or divide damage if it's going to be only 1 damage at most, with reinforced clothing negating even that?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I would say the laws of Physics are pretty mutable in a world where there's magic, humans turning into huge half-wolf-monsters and vampires changing into anything. Where would all that mass go/come from anyway? Arguing on square cube law is not a solid point IMO. Weirder things are happening than super strong mosquitoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 07-17-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:19:43-07:00","id":1117205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117197#post1117197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true, but then again it's pretty dumb that when using any creature with a size of 0, and most size 1, you would have 0 Strength or Brawl. You would be using a chance die pretty much always. Seems too weak to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't. Rats and Bats both have 1 Strength, though Bats have a dot of Brawl. Plus the swarm ignores Defense. It's a small dicepool but it's not a chance die. And you can use other abilities to make it so you're doing Aggravated damage, or Lethal without them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-17-2017, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:33:19-07:00","id":1117209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117205#post1117205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't. Rats and Bats both have 1 Strength, though Bats have a dot of Brawl. Plus the swarm ignores Defense. It's a small dicepool but it's not a chance die. And you can use other abilities to make it so you're doing Aggravated damage, or Lethal without them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So turning into 1 rat would be almost as powerful as 100 rats? Surprise attack as a rat has the same damage potential as a swarm of them? If you ask me, I would rather take on the 1 rat. It is true that changing it to aggravated is pretty powerful, but why bother since most of the time you'd still do more damage in Vampire form, no need to spend merit points. Bear in mind that the Swarm has no &quot;weapon bonus&quot;. I've found that most damage by far come from that +1 to +4 that weapons/claws/teeth give.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:43:16-07:00","id":1117213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117209#post1117209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So turning into 1 rat would be almost as powerful as 100 rats? Surprise attack as a rat has the same damage potential as a swarm of them? If you ask me, I would rather take on the 1 rat. It is true that changing it to aggravated is pretty powerful, but why bother since most of the time you'd still do more damage in Vampire form, no need to spend merit points. Bear in mind that the Swarm has no &quot;weapon bonus&quot;. I've found that most damage by far come from that +1 to +4 that weapons/claws/teeth give.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try not to confuse powerful for 'damage dealing.' Like I said, it's better for harassment and utility use. 'The swarm limits visibility and hearing, and causes panic in all those present. Everyone within the swarm\u2019s area suffers the persistent Distracted Condition (see p.302) until they get away. With Storyteller discretion, a swarm may have other features suited to the swarm animal. For example, rats should be better at biting through barricades.'<br /> <br /> With a more normal opponent you can just follow them and eat away at them or your buddies take them out while they can't see a route to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:44:02-07:00","id":1117214,"title":"","content":"The RAW is pretty clear, but it's also nonsensical. When you attack with a swarm of rats you attack with all who are in range of the victim. It makes a lot more sense to me to use the vampire's own stats as they project them through the strength of the swarm rather than having a single rat do a surprise attack when you control hundreds of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:02:17-07:00","id":1117226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117213#post1117213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Try not to confuse powerful for 'damage dealing.' Like I said, it's better for harassment and utility use. 'The swarm limits visibility and hearing, and causes panic in all those present. Everyone within the swarm\u2019s area suffers the persistent Distracted Condition (see p.302) until they get away. With Storyteller discretion, a swarm may have other features suited to the swarm animal. For example, rats should be better at biting through barricades.'<br /> <br /> With a more normal opponent you can just follow them and eat away at them or your buddies take them out while they can't see a route to escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Distracted condition is not that big of a deal:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Constant confusion and distractions buffet your character from all sides. She cannot take extended actions, and suffers a \u20132 die penalty to all rolls involving perception, concentration, and precision. This Condition does not grant a Beat when resolved.<br /> Possible Sources: Being in a swarm.<br /> Resolution: Leaving the swarm. Beat: n/a </div> </div> </div>It's kinda catch-all with the whole precision thing, but I read it so that basically it means you have a hard time trying to study for your next exam or pick a lock or do brain surgery WHILE YOU ARE COVERED IN AN SWARM OF CLAWS AND BEAKS RIPPING AT YOUR FLESH AND PECKING OUT YOUR EYES, OMG MY EYES!<br /> <br /> But yeah, I guess I just lack imagination and think too much like &quot;stand there and hit stuff&quot; to see the utility of it outside of straight up combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:02:53-07:00","id":1117227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117214#post1117214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The RAW is pretty clear, but it's also nonsensical. When you attack with a swarm of rats you attack with all who are in range of the victim. It makes a lot more sense to me to use the vampire's own stats as they project them through the strength of the swarm rather than having a single rat do a surprise attack when you control hundreds of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, a swarm is a writhing mass of animals, they're not all going to be attacking from the best angle with the skills of a vampire with martial arts, even hundreds of rats aren't going to all be able to cover an individual, most would just be barely hanging on. I suppose in the best case, you would use piranha who would have more Brawl or Strength.<br /> <br /> Nothing says they can't use Willpower or Physical Intensity, or Frenzy to take advantage of the Blood Potency bonus to add a lot to the minimal dicepool a swarm of small animals could take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117226#post1117226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kinda catch-all with the whole precision thing, but I read it so that basically it means you have a hard time trying to study for your next exam or pick a lock or do brain surgery WHILE YOU ARE COVERED IN AN SWARM OF CLAWS AND BEAKS RIPPING AT YOUR FLESH AND PECKING OUT YOUR EYES, OMG MY EYES!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ravens and crows are too big to be made with Swarm Form. Incidentally, a forceful attack like that would likely be represented by a use of Willpower, which would add 3 to the dicepool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yeah, I guess I just lack imagination and think too much like &quot;stand there and hit stuff&quot; to see the utility of it outside of straight up combat. </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the frustration, but this is the same forum where we constantly hear refrains of, 'That's too powerful it can't do that.' In regards to Efficient Killer, eliminating Athletics from Defense, doing Aggravated with a bite attack and various Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Apologies, I was getting rude. 07-17-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:11:40-07:00","id":1117233,"title":"","content":"Should also point out that werewolves who have forms with tough natural armor would hard counter the rat thing; seriously brings down the reliability of the swarm attacks. And unlike a bunch of other types of armor, it's the werewolf in its entirity in that specific form that's armored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:41:56-07:00","id":1117253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117227#post1117227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ravens and crows are too big to be made with Swarm Form.....<br /> <br /> I appreciate the frustration....</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh damn, I actually thought ravens were still size 1. I guess I portrayed that power wrong in my game, I had the Gangrel turn into a flock of ravens <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. It's a good thing that my players don't read any of the rules, much less the forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Strangely I've been enjoying this bout of rule-interpreting, so don't worry I'm not offended or anything. Been interesting thinking about this actually.<br /> <br /> I was remembering one more thing about the Swarm Form that had me wondering and it's this passage:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternately, a success may instead allow the vampire to take one Vitae from a victim. </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you look at it, it might support you arguments nofather. Now, does that mean that no matter how many successes you get, you only get 1 Vitae? Or does it mean that each success would give 1 Vitae? Which would incidentally always cause 1 lethal to living beings. Either way, that would pretty much always be the most sensible move from the Vamps perspective, since it's pretty unlikely to get more than 1 success even when using Willpower, if you only have like 4 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:56:51-07:00","id":1117261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117253#post1117253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how you look at it, it might support you arguments nofather. Now, does that mean that no matter how many successes you get, you only get 1 Vitae? Or does it mean that each success would give 1 Vitae? Which would incidentally always cause 1 lethal to living beings. Either way, that would pretty much always be the most sensible move from the Vamps perspective, since it's pretty unlikely to get more than 1 success even when using Willpower, if you only have like 4 dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feeding through violence is apparently not that efficient a thing to do, even in human form, a violent feeding only gives you 1 Vitae. You need the grapple + feed move combo to get more per turn, and then it's limited by your Blood Potency. There should probably be some sort of Swarm Form-only grapple that allows you to drain more but requires focusing on an individual in the swarm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T10:10:20-07:00","id":1117266,"title":"","content":"Food for thought, RE: &quot;werewolves, having access to the Shadow, are at a permanent advantage over vampires who are stuck in regular space.&quot;<br /> <br /> 1. Yes, absolutely, being able to slip from Point A to Point B without attracting any mortal attention is a powerful tool.<br /> <br /> 2. On the other hand, though... access isn't the same thing as control. There are plenty of things that go bump in the Shadowy night, like potent spirits, that have their own agendas and might be disinclined to let werewolves trespass without challenge, especially if they're congregating around vampires as sources of tasty Essence. <br /> <br /> Spirits are an integral part of the Werewolf story, but that doesn't always make them Werewolf assets; they can be, or they can be violent enemies, depending upon the needs of the story and what would make for more dramatic narrative. (And Helions still hate the half-fleshed for what they did to Luna's lover.)<br /> <br /> Imagine: the Prince has been at her wits' end, trying to figure out how the local Lupines have been vanishing and reappearing seemingly at will as they &quot;clean up&quot; her smuggling operation... until one night, Elysium receives a visit from a smiling young man with bloody knives for teeth (read: Spirit-Claimed by an <i>ensih </i>of [pick your poison]). He claims to be an emissary of others like himself, and offers to protect them from the wolves' mysterious back-and-forth travel. In exchange? Why, he just wants them to... <i>adjust</i> their feeding habits. (Read: risk Humanity to generate more Essence of its preferred type.) That kind of choice - risking your Humanity &amp; the Masquerade, or risking waking up to wolves in your haven - is the stuff of compelling drama; why not exploit it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T10:41:01-07:00","id":1117276,"title":"","content":"On swarms: as much as I like the VtR:2nd corebook, I'd suggest that Onyx Path really nailed the mechanics of swarms more effectively in Demon (pg. 179) and in Beast (pg. 126). If I were running another Vampire game, I'd probably adapt Swarm Form to the following:<br /> <br /> - Radius is two yards per dot of Blood Potency<br /> - Speed is double normal; move in three dimensions; fit through any opening<br /> - Inflict one bashing damage per turn to everything in the swarm's radius OR condense on one target &amp; inflict lethal damage/drain Vitae equal to Blood Potency<br /> - Armor effective against swarm damage only if covering the whole body, and even then only at half normal rating<br /> - Everyone else in the swarm's radius takes -2 penalty to all actions; may trigger Breaking Points for the entophobic<br /> - Taking damage reduces radius proportionally (take half damage, shrink to half size)<br /> - Non-area damage capped at 1 (normal) or 2 (Exceptional Success)<br /> - On any turn in which the swarm condenses, these caps double (max. 2 normal, 4 Exceptional); easier to squish a lot of tiny things when they're all tightly grouped together<br /> - Full damage from fire, sunlight, area attacks<br /> - Celerity &amp; Resilience work as normal<br /> - Vigor passive adds one yard of extra radius per dot; Vigor active adds to effective Blood Potency for that turn when condensing<br /> - Can't use Claws of the Unholy<br /> - Only one physical &quot;active&quot; effect per turn (<i>e.g.</i> if using Vigor active, can't use Celerity active)*<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> *Watsonian explanation: each of those tiny, gnashing bodies can't channel the power of the Curse as effectively as the vampire's &quot;real&quot; form, and/or the vampire's power is already taxed by independently coordinating so many moving parts at once.<br /> <br /> Doylist explanation: being a swarm already makes it very tough for most foes to cause you harm. It should be an overall buff, to reflect the XP spent on the Merit, but the combination of automatic lethal damage (Vigor active) + swarm immunity + preemption in case someone brought a grenade or a flamethrower (Celerity active) seems too much; pick two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","user":"AmusedByIrony","date":". 07-17-2017, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T07:15:08-07:00","id":1117713,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13570\" data-vbnamecard=\"13570\">AmusedByIrony</a>, thanks for that. I recently noticed the size restriction as well recently and was disappointed as I'll need to soon use the form or similar Animalism displays.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's a potential fix:<br /> <b>Murder of Crows (2 point Merit) [Swarm]</b><br /> Most Kindred use <i>Murder of Crows</i> to dissolve into a writhing, screeching mass of flapping carrion birds, but it can enable any other, similarly sized creatures to be assumed as per Swarm Form. Your ability to dissolve your flesh into a swarm includes larger creatures up to Size 2. Doing so costs an additional Vitae but brings several benefits: the size of your swarm doubles, and if damage dealt to it by a single attack is not sufficient to kill a member of the selected species then that damage is ignored instead of reducing your health per the limits of Swarm Form. <br /> <br /> I can also easily see a 1-point merit that enables vampires to take non-predatory forms, so you can get your swarms of butterflies or whatnot.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T07:31:11-07:00","id":1117720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117266#post1117266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine: the Prince has been at her wits' end, trying to figure out how the local Lupines have been vanishing and reappearing seemingly at will as they &quot;clean up&quot; her smuggling operation... until one night, Elysium receives a visit from a smiling young man with bloody knives for teeth (read: Spirit-Claimed by an <i>ensih </i>of [pick your poison]). He claims to be an emissary of others like himself, and offers to protect them from the wolves' mysterious back-and-forth travel. In exchange? Why, he just wants them to... <i>adjust</i> their feeding habits. (Read: risk Humanity to generate more Essence of its preferred type.) That kind of choice - risking your Humanity &amp; the Masquerade, or risking waking up to wolves in your haven - is the stuff of compelling drama; why not exploit it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably go with a strix or Tengu totem for a pack, like in Japan. From a vampire player point of view, Humanity isn't something you want to risk for something as simple and frequent as feeding. Literally a few bad rolls and your character is gone. Harmony doesn't have that as an option, and disharmony is as part of the game as spirits.<br /> <br /> Plus as much as they'd want to survive, no vampire domain is so unified it wouldn't have someone entirely willing to sell the claimed's bane, ban and place of habitation if it meant their enemies died instead of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-18-2017, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:15:26-07:00","id":1117743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117233#post1117233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should also point out that werewolves who have forms with tough natural armor would hard counter the rat thing; seriously brings down the reliability of the swarm attacks. And unlike a bunch of other types of armor, it's the werewolf in its entirity in that specific form that's armored.</div> </div> </div> </div> Protean claws ignore armor. Rat swarm + agg claws will bypass all that. Now, you could use the one Glory Rage gift that reduces damage; that'd work. But that also costs essence per attack unless you're in a Death Rage. And if the werewolf goes into a Death Rage? No one is winning that. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:22:33-07:00","id":1117749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117039#post1117039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also besides editing after the fact you have to keep in mind prophetic power that would get a tip off long before something that including Knowing Practice of Fate or Time Arcanums, the Omen Numina and Cahalith Prophetic Dreams?</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't forget Mehket dreams and cruac rituals. Vamps get seers too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:36:12-07:00","id":1117763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117743#post1117743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Protean claws ignore armor. Rat swarm + agg claws will bypass all that. Now, you could use the one Glory Rage gift that reduces damage; that'd work. But that also costs essence per attack unless you're in a Death Rage. And if the werewolf goes into a Death Rage? No one is winning that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so you have AP2. K. So, question, would you have the ability to manifest claws like that as a swarm, do you have the ability to manifest a natural weapon in that manner? And why is the vampire doing aggravated, the vampire must be in Frenzy for it to be agg.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:50:40-07:00","id":1117773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117763#post1117763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so you have AP2. K. So, question, would you have the ability to manifest claws like that as a swarm, do you have the ability to manifest a natural weapon in that manner? And why is the vampire doing aggravated, the vampire must be in Frenzy for it to be agg.</div> </div> </div> </div> Riding the wave is quite a common tactic for gangrel, given that its a way to supplement their clan weakness, so assuming that we're riding the wave for the frenzy bonuses isn't a stretch.<br /> <br /> As for the swarm form with Protean 2 / 4 abilities? Rose, back when she was vampire developer, said that she would allow it so. In general, the game is permissive rather than restrictive. And, to be fair, it is rather balanced in terms of vampire abilities - Dominate 1, Majesty 2, Nightmare 2, Obfuscate are all basically powerful enough to shut down an entire combat on their own, including one that includes an animal swarm that has a single mind behind it. There's nothing that says you lose access to your bought powers when in swarm form as well; WoD games are permissive, not restictive by nature. I can't think of a single reason that it should be barred beyond some STs feeling its too powerful*. Given the existance of things like Efficent Killer, however? I personally don't think we really can say that its too powerful for 2e.<br /> <br /> <br /> * It might not make sense to have unholy talons if you're taking the form of a critter that doesn't have claws, but for the sake of argument, I'm going to pretend that we do. A swarm of flying critters with talons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-18-2017, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:54:41-07:00","id":1117776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117773#post1117773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Riding the wave is quite a common tactic for gangrel, given that its a way to supplement their clan weakness, so assuming that we're riding the wave for the bonuses isn't a stretch.<br /> <br /> As for the swarm form with Protean 2 / 4 abilities? Rose, back when she was vampire developer, said that she would allow it so. In general, the game is permissive rather than restrictive. And, to be fair, it is rather balanced in terms of vampire abilities - Dominate 1, Majesty 2, Nightmare 2, Obfuscate are all basically powerful enough to shut down an entire combat on their own, including one that includes an animal swarm that has a single mind behind it. There's nothing that says you lose access to your bought powers when in swarm form as well. I can't think of a single reason that it should be barred beyond some STs feeling its too powerful. Given the existance of things like Efficent Killer, however? I personally don't think we really can say that its too powerful for 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I was just confused on making the claws, since to me made no sense to apply it while as a swarm because... you aren't really weilding protean claws, but I suppose that's fine. As in, it's mostly just a &quot;physicals&quot; thing, but eh, magic. Would point out that the swarm is probably going to focus on bites as opposed to claws, but I suppose there's a plan somewhere to get bite attacks along the line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:06:08-07:00","id":1117788,"title":"","content":"Well, when it comes to swarm forms, I always think in terms of a bird or bat swarm, and they definitely can use their talons to scratch and attack with. Either way, I'm just commenting on the rules, not on who'd really &quot;win.&quot; Really, if you had someone with that much Protean get into combat with a werewolf? Just go up and out. Even werewolves with Impossible Spoor are going to be hard pressed to track a bat when their spoor is a mile in the sky and can sleep by merging with a building or tall tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:16:16-07:00","id":1117793,"title":"","content":"We had someone do the maths about this, I thought it was Almarck. In individual fights that is what you need, a vampire who can go all out at once. Because once you get to the next turn the vampire is on the decline. Werewolves are very efficient Essence-users, while vampires aren't, and attempts to get it back hinder their fighting ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:31:40-07:00","id":1117801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1117793#post1117793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had someone do the maths about this, I thought it was Almarck. In individual fights that is what you need, a vampire who can go all out at once. Because once you get to the next turn the vampire is on the decline. Werewolves are very efficient Essence-users, while vampires aren't, and attempts to get it back hinder their fighting ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not me; I was doing speed calculations since I was trying to match them against scifi supersoldiers, not vampires and 1vs1 showdowns (also how fights versus fansplats that turn into kaiju monsters would turn out, but that's beside the point)<br /> <br /> I think it was Pendragon or Chris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:28:37-07:00","id":1132181,"title":"","content":"I hate two things even about 2ed. <br /> 1) Gauru time is toops short and make you pay a lot for either Stamina or PU. It is not only about vampires but for them it'seems easy to use this flaw thanks to Celerity. <br /> 2) Lifespan. AFAIK the opportunity of long life (immortality?) won high PU-level was not retconed in 2ed but it wasn'the normally described.Hence, in later vampire book (forgot the title sorry) there wasn'the even example of longtime werewolf companion for vampire (whole all other gamelines - makes, demons, etc - were representedescribed, only werewolves, mummies and hunters weren't)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:40:04-07:00","id":1132186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132181#post1132181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate two things even about 2ed. <br /> 1) Gauru time is toops short and make you pay a lot for either Stamina or PU. It is not only about vampires but for them it'seems easy to use this flaw thanks to Celerity. <br /> 2) Lifespan. AFAIK the opportunity of long life (immortality?) won high PU-level was not retconed in 2ed but it wasn'the normally described.Hence, in later vampire book (forgot the title sorry) there wasn'the even example of longtime werewolf companion for vampire (whole all other gamelines - makes, demons, etc - were representedescribed, only werewolves, mummies and hunters weren't)</div> </div> </div> </div>For the first point, there is a werewolf gift that extends Garou with an amount of extra turns equal to the Garou's honor.<br /> <br /> For the second point, it was a bummer to not see werewolves and mummies (this one even moreso) in that part of 1000 years of night. However, I can think of only one Hunter organization that can live as long as vampires, and that would be the Lucifuge; for replicating their powers I would suggest Theban Sorcery or Cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:48:30-07:00","id":1132192,"title":"","content":"As for me, it could be nice (and more logical btw) Gauru time would be Willpower + PU, not Stamina+PU. <br /> Yep. It was exactlying lazy writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T08:05:15-07:00","id":1132216,"title":"","content":"I think they were trying to avoid double-dipping. Resolve + Composure already comes up in control rolls, as well as the roll that gives you an extra turn. Having it be based on stamina instead gives werewolves an incentive to get stamina and avoids situations like tertiary physical being an optimal build for werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T12:00:26-07:00","id":1132335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132186#post1132186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the first point, there is a werewolf gift that extends <b><i>Gauru</i></b> with an amount of extra turns equal to the <b>Uratha</b>'s honor.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-21-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T12:05:12-07:00","id":1132337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves#post1114913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In NWoD, I have never actually had or seen werewolves fight vampires. How is it? I have seen plenty of vampire vs. werewolf fights in VtM, which usually didn't turn out well for the vampires. What's it like? And why do they fight if they did? WtF virtually has nothing on vampires or even VtR. It's out of the a werewolf's scope.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Werewolves commonly have access to powers that dwarf those of your typical vampire. It takes the likes of Theban Sorcery or Cruac to achieve similar feats of supernatural might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T12:23:39-07:00","id":1132351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132335#post1132335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emphasis mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quotes are automatically put in italics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T13:32:36-07:00","id":1132374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132216#post1132216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they were trying to avoid double-dipping. Resolve + Composure already comes up in control rolls, as well as the roll that gives you an extra turn. Having it be based on stamina instead gives werewolves an incentive to get stamina and avoids situations like tertiary physical being an optimal build for werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Thus averase start char has 3-5 turns in Gauru than Rage is only option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T15:59:14-07:00","id":1132421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132335#post1132335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emphasis mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I get for having played Apocalypse and Forsaken. My mind jumbles up the terms. Thanks for correcting me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T16:43:41-07:00","id":1132431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132374#post1132374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Thus averase start char has 3-5 turns in Gauru than Rage is only option.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Gauru is <i>really </i>powerful. Even in one turn you can wipe out an entire group of humans using the Down &amp; Dirty rules and come out without a scratch. In 5 turns most 'elite' opponents should be dead. Not counting big bosses, of course.<br /> <br /> Plus there's always Kuruth. The downsides of it have been diminished. You're not likely to attack packmates with it, and if you have an Elodoth they can drag you out. It potentially extends your time by 10 minutes to 12 hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-21-2017, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T17:20:57-07:00","id":1132443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132431#post1132431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, Gauru is <i>really </i>powerful. Even in one turn you can wipe out an entire group of humans using the Down &amp; Dirty rules and come out without a scratch. In 5 turns most 'elite' opponents should be dead. Not counting big bosses, of course.<br /> <br /> Plus there's always Kuruth. The downsides of it have been diminished. You're not likely to attack packmates with it, and if you have an Elodoth they can drag you out. It potentially extends your time by 10 minutes to 12 hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I've seen Irraka using Eviscerate to score like 19 successes in brawl with the rote action in Gauru against a BP 5 elder.<br /> <br /> The way that my Hunter in Darkness deals with Pure intruding into his turf is make them get lost in it for a whole day after inciting them to Kuruth; assuming that they all have different PU, one's gonna try to eat the others after they collapse post death rage - then pick the last one(s) off when they pass out. They give our place a wide vert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-21-2017, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T21:02:27-07:00","id":1132501,"title":"","content":"Kuruth alsp has the advanfage pf turning the Essence costs of some abilities to 0. You can spam lots of buffs as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T22:23:35-07:00","id":1132508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132192#post1132192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for me, it could be nice (and more logical btw) Gauru time would be Willpower + PU, not Stamina+PU.<br /> Yep. It was exactlying lazy writing.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>No, it was make for players of Uratha characters to <i>wonder</i> if they should use Kuruth option</b>. In <b>Apocalypse</b>, Crinos was totally free of restrictions - so anyone was using it any time, how long it takes. In <b>Forsaken</b> 2E, Gauru Form you can freely takes for few turns and then <i>then</i> you risk Basu-Im ( Hard Rage ) - risk murdering your packmaters. Yes, it was made so Uratha would be affraid of their own powers - it's in the most basic build of the game. 'We are Uratha, strongest predators of the world - but also most savage monsters. Do not cross our paths, as we cannot assure we will control ourselves.'<br /> <br /> On the other hand, even those typical 4-5 turns in controlled Gauru for most time is enough. Hell, on our last Viking Era game session, my starting Uratha PCs pack wiped Ancille ( that is written right? ) coterie of Nosferatu from Lancea Sanctum in medieval monastery. BUT as vampires were using Silver weapons ( they were hunting Uratha for some time now ), players Blood Talon Rahu <i>almost</i> die. Good times! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:15:24-07:00","id":1132651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132508#post1132508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>No, it was make for players of Uratha characters to <i>wonder</i> if they should use Kuruth option</b>. In <b>Apocalypse</b>, Crinos was totally free of restrictions - so anyone was using it any time, how long it takes. In <b>Forsaken</b> 2E, Gauru Form you can freely takes for few turns and then <i>then</i> you risk Basu-Im ( Hard Rage ) - risk murdering your packmaters. Yes, it was made so Uratha would be affraid of their own powers - it's in the most basic build of the game. 'We are Uratha, strongest predators of the world - but also most savage monsters. Do not cross our paths, as we cannot assure we will control ourselves.'<br /> <br /> On the other hand, even those typical 4-5 turns in controlled Gauru for most time is enough. Hell, on our last Viking Era game session, my starting Uratha PCs pack wiped Ancille ( that is written right? ) coterie of Nosferatu from Lancea Sanctum in medieval monastery. BUT as vampires were using Silver weapons ( they were hunting Uratha for some time now ), players Blood Talon Rahu <i>almost</i> die. Good times! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. How did you do it? Gifts, tactics? Could you tell more please","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T11:20:33-07:00","id":1132712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132651#post1132651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. How did you do it? Gifts, tactics? Could you tell more please</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not know what to tell more - Nosferatu vamps used mainly <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124715#post1124715\">Nightmare to induce Death Rage on Uratha</a> and attacked using Silver Weapons with Vigor on ( best dicepool was Strength 4 + Weaponry 4 + Vigor 4 ). Even then, Rahu declare using of his Facets that give him 8-Again on attacks and &lt;Not remembering Renown&gt; extra Health box, on top of Gauru Health bonus boxes. By being attacked by only 2 vamps like that he was mechanically 'dead' ( last box of Aggravated filled ) in second turn, but give him chance to survive if players will do something. One of two other wolves - both Ithaeur - asked one of Vikings crew members to sacrifice his life - and used sacrifice to bargain with local Spirit of Restoration that used his Numina to cure &lt;Rank&gt; numbers of Aggravated damage on Rahu. AFTER whole pack made total massacre in Death Rage they got from Rahu's Health filled. Oh, it looked I could say more about this fight, in the end. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-22-2017, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T11:46:06-07:00","id":1132728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132508#post1132508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, even those typical 4-5 turns in controlled Gauru for most time is enough. Hell, on our last Viking Era game session, my starting Uratha PCs pack wiped Ancille ( that is written right? ) coterie of Nosferatu from Lancea Sanctum in medieval monastery. BUT as vampires were using Silver weapons ( they were hunting Uratha for some time now ), players Blood Talon Rahu <i>almost</i> die. Good times! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's Ancilla (singular) and Ancillae (plural).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132712#post1132712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do not know what to tell more - Nosferatu vamps used mainly <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124715#post1124715\">Nightmare to induce Death Rage on Uratha</a> and attacked using Silver Weapons with Vigor on ( best dicepool was Strength 4 + Weaponry 4 + Vigor 4 ). Even then, Rahu declare using of his Facets that give him 8-Again on attacks and &lt;Not remembering Renown&gt; extra Health box, on top of Gauru Health bonus boxes. By being attacked by only 2 vamps like that he was mechanically 'dead' ( last box of Aggravated filled ) in second turn, but give him chance to survive if players will do something. One of two other wolves - both Ithaeur - asked one of Vikings crew members to sacrifice his life - and used sacrifice to bargain with local Spirit of Restoration that used his Numina to cure &lt;Rank&gt; numbers of Aggravated damage on Rahu. AFTER whole pack made total massacre in Death Rage they got from Rahu's Health filled. Oh, it looked I could say more about this fight, in the end. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically a deus ex machina, albeit an appropriate one. Personally I would have made that spirit unable to equate a mortal life to that of an Uratha, and asked for an Uratha sacrifice. What's the point in wasting blood and inducing death rage before hand if you'd likely get that result by nicking them with silver already?<br /> <br /> Yes, hunting Uratha with silver is relatively easier, assuming you can survive a potential whole pack of them going berserk on you. The best chance Nosferatu have is picking on the pack one by one with Obfuscate. Vigor would've fucked up their weaponry easier than silver bullets crumble on impact, mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:14:17-07:00","id":1132765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132728#post1132728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So,basically a deus ex machina, albeit an appropriate one. Personally I would have made that spirit unable to equate a mortal life to that of an Uratha, and asked for an Uratha sacrifice. What's the point in wasting blood and inducing death rage before hand if you'd likely get that result by nicking them with silver already?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, not the best fight tbh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> At least, if this sacrifice is a 'canon' method.<br /> The best Forsaken trick against vampires<br /> TONGUE OF FLAME (PURITY)<br /> The Uratha who possesses this Facet is mistress of flame and<br /> smoke. She is a fire-walker to whom the blaze pays obeisance.<br /> Cost: Varies<br /> The Uratha gains Influence (Fire) equal to her dots in<br /> Purity. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit.<br /> Her dice pool for Influence (Fire) rolls is equal to her Presence<br /> + Empathy + Purity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:18:35-07:00","id":1132768,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's a nice one. Werewolves really have a lot of options better than confronting superpowered opponents head on after giving them time to arm themselves with silver weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:34:53-07:00","id":1132780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132768#post1132768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that's a nice one. Werewolves really have a lot of options better than confronting superpowered opponents head on after giving them time to arm themselves with silver weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair those are new-ish players to RPG ( they are high school students, playing 1 year under me as their first ST ) and Vikings Uratha were 'surprised' there are vampires in the monastery in first place. They had one ominous, unclear vision before voyage - nothing really directly pointing 'Here will be vampires'. But good to know anti-vampire Facet - will use it in our modern setting crossover also, against modern Uppsala Archbishop. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-22-2017, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:37:52-07:00","id":1132782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132780#post1132780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair those are new-ish players to RPG ( they are high school students, playing 1 year under me as ST ) and Vikings were 'surprised' there are vampires in the monastery - They had one ominous, unclear vision before voyage - nothing really directly pointing 'Here will be vampires'. But good to know anti-vampire Facet - will use it in our modern setting crossover also, against modern Uppsalla Archbishop. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I gotcha, and I can completely understand that sort of playstyle, even knowingly, I just hope they came away from the battle ready to plan better next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T15:14:11-07:00","id":1132816,"title":"","content":"Btw, what about vampires in Smoke-form (Protean 4 or 5 IIRC)? Is it still 'matter' or vampire become kind of Astral-thing?<br /> I mean, could they be harmed by <br /> BARGHEST, which allows &quot;While in Gauru, Urshul, and Urhan, she is able to attack such Twilight beings and damage them by spending 1 Essence per scene.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T15:19:46-07:00","id":1132817,"title":"","content":"Primeval Miasma, Protean 5. The vampire becomes intangible but not actually ephemeral. If they did they wouldn't be visible at all nor incapable of passing through solid objects. The Barghest Facet would not do a thing. Same thing with Strix unless the ST is generous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T15:24:16-07:00","id":1132818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132817#post1132817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The vampire becomes intangible but not actually ephemeral.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, only fire?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T15:24:44-07:00","id":1132819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132817#post1132817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primeval Miasma, Protean 5. The vampire becomes intangible but not actually ephemeral. If they did they wouldn't be visible at all nor incapable of passing through solid objects. The Barghest Facet would not do a thing. Same thing with Strix unless the ST is generous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if they can damage the Vampire in those forms, they can still drain Willpower or deal extra damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T15:27:08-07:00","id":1132820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132818#post1132818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, only fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire, sunlight, and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">Pseshkf</a>.<br /> Acquired banes should also work but the very few actually damaging banes only deal a set amount of bashing.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132819#post1132819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if they can damage the Vampire in those forms, they can still drain Willpower or deal extra damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically no. The text for Barghest specifies corporeal undead in order to drain WP or deal +2L.<br /> <br /> Second edit: Vampires using Primeval Miasma and Strix fall between the cracks. Barghest is written to affect either ephemeral entities or corporeal undead. I don't think the writer was aware that non-ephemeral, non-corporeal undead is a thing so I think it's perfectly reasonable to extend Barghest's effects on ephemerals to incorporeal entities as well, similar to Pseshkf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-22-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T16:02:17-07:00","id":1132828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132818#post1132818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, only fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wind and water, actually. If you have Manipulate Air or Wind you can just put them in a bottle. Get a fetish or talen for Blood Influence and you can do whatever you want.<br /> <br /> Fire for pure damage, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-22-2017, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T17:33:44-07:00","id":1132854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132828#post1132828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wind and water, actually. If you have Manipulate Air or Wind you can just put them in a bottle. Get a fetish or talen for Blood Influence and you can do whatever you want.<br /> <br /> Fire for pure damage, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gonna be a big bottle, cus the miasma won't compress less then the volume of her size. And prolly a Clash of Wills. And b<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">lood </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2260 Vitae as well.<br /> <br /> But yeah, fire for damage. Probably need a lot of purity before it's worth anything though. And even then it's an Influence, ergo storyteller fiat-extraordinary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T17:55:41-07:00","id":1132864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132854#post1132854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Gonna be a big bottle, cus the miasma won't compress less then the volume of her size. And prolly a Clash of Wills. And b<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">lood </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2260 Vitae as well.<br /> <br /> But yeah, fire for damage. Probably need a lot of purity before it's worth anything though. And even then it's an Influence, ergo storyteller fiat-extraordinary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Original size of the vampire?<br /> <br /> Yep, you should not put wolfcub vs elder with 5th Discipline. Uratha are not Beasts or Demons. Anyway, Molotov cocktail reduce necessary Purity to 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T18:08:52-07:00","id":1132871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132864#post1132864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Original size of the vampire?<br /> <br /> Yep, you should not put wolfcub vs elder with 5th Discipline. Uratha are not Beasts or Demons. Anyway, Molotov cocktail reduce necessary Purity to 3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea, so usually size 5 ^_^ <br /> <br /> Yeah that's probably a stupid idea either way for both of them. Yeah Molotovs are nice in that regard ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T19:49:55-07:00","id":1132889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132854#post1132854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna be a big bottle, cus the miasma won't compress less then the volume of her size.</div> </div> </div> </div>A car trunk, maybe? You could just hold it over a fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And prolly a Clash of Wills. </div> </div> </div>Standard defense would be enough, plus their Supernatural Tolerance. There's a misconception about Clash of Wills that it acts as some sort of extra resistance roll. It's really when two conflicting powers clash. Obfuscate vs Auspex, for instance. If someone was trying to turn the smoke into a vampire, sure because that goes directly against the power of the spell, but controlling the smoke wouldn't provoke any Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And blood \u2260 Vitae as well. </div> </div> </div>That's true, chemically. But it's likely close enough for spirits.<br /> <br /> Having checked out the ability, however, and seen that it turns it into <i>smoke </i>and not mist, which was what I thought, the Water one wouldn't be an acceptable alternative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yeah, fire for damage. Probably need a lot of purity before it's worth anything though. And even then it's an Influence, ergo storyteller fiat-extraordinary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR] </div> </div> </div>Four dots is really the maximum you'd need in a fight, providing you weren't dealing with a swarm or something. With four, you just create fire on the vampire. But with 3 dots you could take an existing fire, like a torch in your hand, and have it lash out and burn the target. With 2 dots, you could do something more reasonable with it, like if you threw a molotov and missed, have it spread to the vampire providing they were close. But if you hit them with a molotov, you could just use 1 dot to Strengthen it, doing more damage.<br /> <br /> You don't even need the Gift to do it, though. Influences are available via talen, and if you're hunting vampires you'd have reason to stock up. May as well go the extra mile and get some Sun Influence talens. If vampires are going to the lengths of making weapons of pure silver, that's a reasonable expectation.<br /> <br /> I like these things but they're the type of ability I would fall into a trap of using all the time. One day I'll have my fire breathing werewolf, but until then he's commanding cars to run over people and killing vampires during the day, like a normal person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-22-2017, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T21:40:08-07:00","id":1132908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132889#post1132889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't even need the Gift to do it, though. Influences are available via talen, and if you're hunting vampires you'd have reason to stock up. May as well go the extra mile and get some Sun Influence talens. If vampires are going to the lengths of making weapons of pure silver, that's a reasonable expectation.<br /> <br /> I like these things but they're the type of ability I would fall into a trap of using all the time. One day I'll have my fire breathing werewolf, but until then he's commanding cars to run over people and killing vampires during the day, like a normal person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: Sunlight influence, I'd let try and put vampires into torpor with create due day-sleep. Basically you make their biology want to tuck in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T05:29:00-07:00","id":1132975,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132889#post1132889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Standard defense would be enough, plus their Supernatural Tolerance. There's a misconception about Clash of Wills that it acts as some sort of extra resistance roll. It's really when two conflicting powers clash. Obfuscate vs Auspex, for instance. If someone was trying to turn the smoke into a vampire, sure because that goes directly against the power of the spell, but controlling the smoke wouldn't provoke any Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone where to dissipate, dilute or press the smoke into a &quot;bottle&quot; then it's surely a power in precise contradiction to another power, so a Clash of Wills should be applicable here. However, dealing damage with Fire Influence would not. But using Wind/Air to press the smoke into a trunk would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's true, chemically. But it's likely close enough for spirits. </div> </div> </div>I just don't agree here, blood is just the normal medium for Vitae to exist in, however breath is another. Chemically it's different, but metaphysically, even more so. If Spirits could manipulate Vitae with &quot;Influence: Blood&quot;, werewolves essence would answer to the same &quot;influence: flesh&quot;. I just don't see Vitae/Essence falling under Blood/Flesh influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Four dots is really the maximum you'd need in a fight, providing you weren't dealing with a swarm or something. With four, you just create fire on the vampire. But with 3 dots you could take an existing fire, like a torch in your hand, and have it lash out and burn the target. With 2 dots, you could do something more reasonable with it, like if you threw a molotov and missed, have it spread to the vampire providing they were close. But if you hit them with a molotov, you could just use 1 dot to Strengthen it, doing more damage.<br /> <br /> You don't even need the Gift to do it, though. Influences are available via talen, and if you're hunting vampires you'd have reason to stock up. May as well go the extra mile and get some Sun Influence talens. If vampires are going to the lengths of making weapons of pure silver, that's a reasonable expectation.<br /> <br /> I like these things but they're the type of ability I would fall into a trap of using all the time. One day I'll have my fire breathing werewolf, but until then he's commanding cars to run over people and killing vampires during the day, like a normal person. </div> </div> </div><br /> While I'm not arguing about the technicalities in how Influence works, its just to arbitrary to use as a good example, because it will work completely different around every gaming table, because the rules guiding them are, quite frankly, missing. In the abstract way, I do agree with your assessment how it works, but we are sure to disagree on the details and workings of the powers when it comes to the actual ruling of it. Influence is by far the worst rule still in CofD, it's insanely arbitrary in how it works. It's an fragment from 1ed that should've got updated long ago.<br /> <br /> Four dots i purity is no small feat or achievement, but perfectly reasonable in a fair fight against an elder vampire, if we're having a white room scenario. But I do not see it that easy to get, that so many people seem to be under the impression that it is.<br /> <br /> But yeah in a warring scenario wolfs Vs. vamps it's reasonable that both sides gets to prepare against their enemies, and Influence Sunlight/Fire etc talens and bargain with spirits is on the table for wolves. An interesting way to root out the vamps are using spirits of curiosity, longing, vengeance and the like to influence the vampires victims to get revenge and tear down their Masques. If every victims brother/sister/mom/friend/coworker etc starts to investigate and being pushed to hunt the vampire, soon it won't really have a blood supply.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T05:58:04-07:00","id":1132980,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"523\" data-vbnamecard=\"523\">Poseur</a> Influences are meant to be subjective because the Shadow is meant to be a subjective and symbolic realm - I don't need copious amounts of justification in order imagine how Influence: Cold may be used to calm someone, just like Influence: Fire could make someone hungry. Lesser spirits tend to be 1 trick ponies, which is something of an advantage actually sentient individuals have over them: they can see a spirit use an influence in a novel way and try to copy the effect, whereas a spirit trying to emulate such a thing would first need to eat the example user. Blood has water in it, and being able to manipulate it could do all sorts of funny things to your organism, like the myriad of gruesome effects that Leukemia can have a tool in someone's body. Likewise, getting a fetish to shift Influence: Water for Influence: Blood is trivial, hell I could even go for Influence: Vitae if you're particularly bothered. And with 3 dots there I can likely have vitae pouring out of the elder's every pore till they get torpid silly, from the shadow, and in a matter of minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T04:56:11-07:00","id":1133734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1132980#post1132980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Influences are meant to be subjective because the Shadow is meant to be a subjective and symbolic realm - I don't need copious amounts of justification in order imagine how Influence: Cold may be used to calm someone, just like Influence: Fire could make someone hungry. Lesser spirits tend to be 1 trick ponies, which is something of an advantage actually sentient individuals have over them: they can see a spirit use an influence in a novel way and try to copy the effect, whereas a spirit trying to emulate such a thing would first need to eat the example user. Blood has water in it, and being able to manipulate it could do all sorts of funny things to your organism, like the myriad of gruesome effects that Leukemia can have a tool in someone's body. Likewise, getting a fetish to shift Influence: Water for Influence: Blood is trivial, hell I could even go for Influence: Vitae if you're particularly bothered. And with 3 dots there I can likely have vitae pouring out of the elder's every pore till they get torpid silly, from the shadow, and in a matter of minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but vitae isn't blood. Not really, blood is just the medium that most vampires use to get it. It's just the easiest method.<br /> <br /> For example, with the fifth dot of Protean you can suffocate someone by going inside of them via the throat, and said kindred can get vitae this way. So, vitae cleary just isn't blood.<br /> <br /> I think because of the Kindred's capabilites of eating souls (which has extended beyond other kindred wit 1000 years of night) Vitae is life condensed into something more or less physical. A kindred can still spend Vitae when they're a sentient cloud of smoke despite the fact that they would have no blood at the time, and the Strix get Vitae from stealing the breath of mortals.<br /> <br /> I also kind of disagree with Influence: Cold bring used to calm people down, or <i>chill them</i> as it were. Of course, I'm a bit more of a literal-minded person so I tend to take things like Influence less subjectively.<br /> <br /> I think I should also mention that simply not having vitae wouldn't put a vampire into torpor. They have to go into the daysleep without enough vitae to wake up to go into torpor. Just emptying a vampire of their vitae would make them hungry.<br /> <br /> Also to note, depending on the vampire sunlight might not Influence them as much as another vampire. Sunlight works better on older and less humane kindred. So if you're busting out Influence: Sunlight expect a surge in neonates, ghouls, and Ordo Dracul with coil of the ascendant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T04:59:07-07:00","id":1133736,"title":"","content":"Also a little addendum. Vitae doesn't easily leave Kindred. The strix ability that automatically takes vitae from people in the surrounding area can't take it from Kindred. It just stops them from spending it for a time (keep in mind that this is a higher shadow potency vitae power if memory serves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T07:42:48-07:00","id":1133787,"title":"","content":"If you don't view Blood as close enough, and need to take literal examples, then just replace our 'Blood Influence' with 'Vitae Influence.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:34:16-07:00","id":1133798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133787#post1133787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't view Blood as close enough, and need to take literal examples, then just replace our 'Blood Influence' with 'Vitae Influence.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring an offhand crossover hook about a powerful spirit of the Divine Fire in Promethean, there's generally been no indication that supernatural resources are viable Influences at the common level. Influence: Vitae is pretty much never going to be a &quot;trivial&quot; thing to have access to outside the context of a specifically-made narrative widget in a setting that hasn't been built with an abnormal bias against Kindred vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:41:47-07:00","id":1133802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133798#post1133798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring an offhand crossover hook about a powerful spirit of the Divine Fire in Promethean, there's generally been no indication that supernatural resources are viable Influences at the common level.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not as if we have a lot of crossover books about this. What Influences do you think would be usable against vampires?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Influence: Vitae is pretty much never going to be a &quot;trivial&quot; thing to have access to outside the context of a specifically-made narrative widget in a setting that hasn't been built with an abnormal bias against Kindred vampires. </div> </div> </div>That's what this thread is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-25-2017, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:52:48-07:00","id":1133811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133802#post1133802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not as if we have a lot of crossover books about this. What Influences do you think would be usable against vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the ones that are usable against people or the world around people.<br /> <br /> There is no need to go more esoteric than that in a discussion of how shapeshifting hunters with access to spirit-magic would fight with life-drinking undead curse-carriers unless you're building a specific story about how having an in with a blood god tilts the conflict in one direction or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what this thread is about. </div> </div> </div>This thread is about vampires versus werewolves, not coming up with contrived and unnecessary ways to stack the universe in a werewolf's favor in such a confrontation.<br /> <br /> A werewolf doesn't need trivial access to Influence over pure Vitae to be able to deal with a vampire old and/or powerful enough to have developed the fifth dot of a clan-specific Discipline and it is disingenuous to act as though such a thing has any bearing on what would pass for a standard confrontation between these entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T09:42:58-07:00","id":1133835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133811#post1133811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the ones that are usable against people or the world around people.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a good point. Regular old Darkness and Hunger spirits would be enough to cripple the enemy and turn them against each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This thread is about vampires versus werewolves, not coming up with contrived and unnecessary ways to stack the universe in a werewolf's favor in such a confrontation. </div> </div> </div>We're not talking about a setting where vampires and werewolves do not stumble across each other and burst into violence that leaves one side incapable of any further violence. We're talking about a setting where both sides know of the other and have devoted enough resources to dealing with the Enemy that they have people of importance in the city wearing silver armor, not even vampires but the humans important to the running of the city. The mayor of the city is wearing silver armor, as are higher-ups in the police department.<br /> <br /> We're four pages in. We passed contrived and unnecessary ways to stack the universe in one side's favor long ago..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A werewolf doesn't need trivial access to Influence over pure Vitae to be able to deal with a vampire old and/or powerful enough to have developed the fifth dot of a clan-specific Discipline and it is disingenuous to act as though such a thing has any bearing on what would pass for a standard confrontation between these entities. </div> </div> </div>Clearly at this point we're not talking about what you consider 'a standard confrontation' between these two entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:44:25-07:00","id":1133853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133835#post1133835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're four pages in. We passed contrived and unnecessary ways to stack the universe in one side's favor long ago..<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Clearly at this point we're not talking about what you consider 'a standard confrontation' between these two entities.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Silver armor is a thing that can </span><i>unambiguously be made and supernaturally empowered</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> in the setting as described</span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">. There doesn't need to be </span><i>the sort of thing that would be a story hook in and of itself</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> occupying a setting to facilitate applied metallurgy and normal spiritual dealmaking the way acquiring direct magical influence over a specific supernatural resource that werewolves and spirits aren't normally written to mess with does.<br /> <br /> A setting where that </span><i>is</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> the case is one that would take more than the death of every participant in the conflict to revert to a state where werewolves don't have easy access to the ability to fuck around with <i>the interior contents of a vampire</i>.<br /> <br /> A setting where Influence: Vitae is not the product of rare circumstances and/or substantial bargains is a setting where werewolves have been given extra resources above and beyond native shapeshifting, access to an entire supernatural dimension, and the abilities and nature of a consummate hunter of extremely dangerous beings for, in this discussion, the express purpose of shutting down a desperately hungry supernatural entity at the height of one of the forms of monstrosity available to it.<br /> <br /> That's <i>contriving a fact about the supernatural landscape that has wider implications for the world</i>, which is a great deal further out from the realm of explicit possibility than &quot;sufficiently influential vampires can afford to get their hands on precious metals to ward off the fast-healing wolf-changers who want to end them.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:49:18-07:00","id":1133854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133734#post1133734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but vitae isn't blood. Not really, blood is just the medium that most vampires use to get it. It's just the easiest method.<br /> <br /> For example, with the fifth dot of Protean you can suffocate someone by going inside of them via the throat, and said kindred can get vitae this way. So, vitae cleary just isn't blood.<br /> <br /> I think because of the Kindred's capabilites of eating souls (which has extended beyond other kindred wit 1000 years of night) Vitae is life condensed into something more or less physical. A kindred can still spend Vitae when they're a sentient cloud of smoke despite the fact that they would have no blood at the time, and the Strix get Vitae from stealing the breath of mortals.<br /> <br /> I also kind of disagree with Influence: Cold bring used to calm people down, or <i>chill them</i> as it were. Of course, I'm a bit more of a literal-minded person so I tend to take things like Influence less subjectively.<br /> <br /> I think I should also mention that simply not having vitae wouldn't put a vampire into torpor. They have to go into the daysleep without enough vitae to wake up to go into torpor. Just emptying a vampire of their vitae would make them hungry.<br /> <br /> Also to note, depending on the vampire sunlight might not Influence them as much as another vampire. Sunlight works better on older and less humane kindred. So if you're busting out Influence: Sunlight expect a surge in neonates, ghouls, and Ordo Dracul with coil of the ascendant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred are physical beings barring Protean 5; they carry vitae in blood, remove the blood, the one deep within their shriveled hearts, and they'll lose vitae. Strix bear no relevance to the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> On the matter of influence, there's published fire spirits that indeed are able to stoke people's hunger because the metaphoric concept of fire as a consumer. I'll re-state it: the Shadow is meant to be subjective and a metaphorical realm.<br /> <br /> On sunlight, we're talking about an elder. It's a rare elder one who's maintained high humanity and recently woke up from torpor, in which case, they'll be easier to confront directly. Vampires can apparently mass produce troops of neonates initiated in esoteric vampiric mysteries. Nah, that's unfeasible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring an offhand crossover hook about a powerful spirit of the Divine Fire in Promethean</div> </div> </div> </div>S'ok, I only need that example. You'll have to agree with me that distilled life essence is far more common than the divine fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-25-2017, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:55:49-07:00","id":1133858,"title":"","content":"I think we should also apply the various covenant advantages in this discussion as well, at least to make it a bit more even.<br /> <br /> The Invictus and Carthians have some of the best social merits hands down, and it can be debated which one beats the other in that regard. So when you deal with vampires, it's not just vampires you'll be dealing with. You'll be dealing with every bit of influence they have.<br /> <br /> Then we have the Ordo Dracul, who are basically vampire scientists. They'be unlocked certain aspects of the Kindred condition: some are absolute terrors on the battlefield, others are stronger against fire and sunlight, some more able to control mortal society, and some have super natural merits not available to kindred. The Ordo also typically get more involved in mortal occult societies as well, so they might have some resources against spirits.<br /> <br /> Then the Circle of the Crone can some entities from another realm, cause storms, mess with ghosts to an extent, and can create havens where everything alive fights their enemies.<br /> <br /> Then we have the Lancea et Sanctum who can pull of miracles to empower kindred warriors, help kindred find safe havens, and even blot out the sun.<br /> <br /> So I don't think this battle should lean incredibly far towards werewolves unless we're pulling out things like Influence Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:56:55-07:00","id":1133859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133854#post1133854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S'ok, I only need that example. You'll have to agree with me that distilled life essence is far more common than the divine fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you want to argue that spirits and ghosts being more common than either means the Idigam's Essence Shaping should be nigh-indistinguishable from an easily-accessible Influence: Ephemera, there's no support for your implicit point that Vitae being common means the kind of spirit that would patronize it would be easier to find than something theoretically awakened by a powerful Firestorm to help a werewolf make a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:00:08-07:00","id":1133861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133859#post1133859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you want to argue that spirits and ghosts being more common than either means the Idigam's Essence Shaping should be nigh-indistinguishable from an easily-accessible Influence: Ephemera, there's no support for your implicit point that Vitae being common means the kind of spirit that would patronize it would be easier to find than something theoretically awakened by a powerful Firestorm to help a werewolf make a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't need to be potent. I just need 1 dot in the relevant influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:01:27-07:00","id":1133862,"title":"","content":"Vampires can bleed themselves dry if they so wish and lose no amount of Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:03:06-07:00","id":1133863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133854#post1133854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kindred are physical beings barring Protean 5; they carry vitae in blood, remove the blood, the one deep within their shriveled hearts, and they'll lose vitae. Strix bear no relevance to the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> On the matter of influence, there's published fire spirits that indeed are able to stoke people's hunger because the metaphoric concept of fire as a consumer. I'll re-state it: the Shadow is meant to be subjective and a metaphorical realm.<br /> <br /> On sunlight, we're talking about an elder. It's a rare elder one who's maintained high humanity and recently woke up from torpor, in which case, they'll be easier to confront directly. Vampires can apparently mass produce troops of neonates initiated in esoteric vampiric mysteries. Nah, that's unfeasible.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Kindred bleed when they're hurt. That doesn't make them lose vitae. Vitae is something a vampire clings to, and it is explicitly stated that vitae acts differently than blood when it leaves the Kindred's body. Stabbing a ghoul doesn't make them lose vitae, so why would making a vampire bleed do that. It takes the fifth dot of Kindred dueling style to cut vitae out of people. I think that should speak for itself.<br /> <br /> 2. As I stated, I'm a bit more literal minded. Just because I said I don't think it should doesn't mean it won't. It's one of the varying reasons why I don't like dealing with spirits in games.<br /> <br /> 3. Coil of the Voivode. There is a scale that causes a mass embrace with the loss of one humanity. Once I get back to my book, I will provide the name of the scale and the page it is on via edit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:09:21-07:00","id":1133866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133858#post1133858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we should also apply the various covenant advantages in this discussion as well, at least to make it a bit more even.<br /> <br /> The Invictus and Carthians have some of the best social merits hands down, and it can be debated which one beats the other in that regard. So when you deal with vampires, it's not just vampires you'll be dealing with. You'll be dealing with every bit of influence they have.<br /> <br /> Then we have the Ordo Dracul, who are basically vampire scientists. They'be unlocked certain aspects of the Kindred condition: some are absolute terrors on the battlefield, others are stronger against fire and sunlight, some more able to control mortal society, and some have super natural merits not available to kindred. The Ordo also typically get more involved in mortal occult societies as well, so they might have some resources against spirits.<br /> <br /> Then the Circle of the Crone can some entities from another realm, cause storms, mess with ghosts to an extent, and can create havens where everything alive fights their enemies.<br /> <br /> Then we have the Lancea et Sanctum who can pull of miracles to empower kindred warriors, help kindred find safe havens, and even blot out the sun.<br /> <br /> So I don't think this battle should lean incredibly far towards werewolves unless we're pulling out things like Influence Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things like temporal power would matter if their antagonists functioned within the same spheres of influences. We've got <i>casual</i> examples of werewolves leaving their human lives behind to the exclusive aim of getting rid of an infestation in their city, and to the lengths of spiritual bargains they would go in order to hunt their quarry to virtual extinction. Which Haven would be safe if a pack went to such lenght as to firebomb them during daylight from the relative comfort of the Shadow with the relevant elemental facets? Vampires have too many weaknesses that are easily exploitable by the apex predators of Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:13:13-07:00","id":1133868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133863#post1133863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Kindred bleed when they're hurt. That doesn't make them lose vitae. Vitae is something a vampire clings to, and it is explicitly stated that vitae acts differently than blood when it leaves the Kindred's body. Stabbing a ghoul doesn't make them lose vitae, so why would making a vampire bleed do that. It takes the fifth dot of Kindred dueling style to cut vitae out of people. I think that should speak for itself.<br /> <br /> 2. As I stated, I'm a bit more literal minded. Just because I said I don't think it should doesn't mean it won't. It's one of the varying reasons why I don't like dealing with spirits in games.<br /> <br /> 3. Coil of the Voivode. There is a scale that causes a mass embrace with the loss of one humanity. Once I get back to my book, I will provide the name of the scale and the page it is on via edit.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. LOL no. They explicitly do not. It requires an expenditure of WP in order to give such an effect.<br /> <br /> 2. Your cognitive preference are dully noted.<br /> <br /> 3. Mass embrace a pack of murderous quasi revenants. Sure that'll be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:17:00-07:00","id":1133871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133866#post1133866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Things like temporal power would matter if their antagonists functioned within the same spheres of influences. We've got <i>casual</i> examples of werewolves leaving their human lives behind to the exclusive aim of getting rid of an infestation in their city, and to the lengths of spiritual bargains they would go in order to hunt their quarry to virtual extinction. Which Haven would be safe if a pack went to such lenght as to firebomb them during daylight from the relative comfort of the Shadow with the relevant elemental facets? Vampires have too many weaknesses that are easily exploitable by the apex predators of Pangaea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the Iron Masters are one of the Tribes, yes temporal influence does matter. And for the Shadow, there will be spirits that will fight alongside the Kindred. Spirits of paranoia, blood, darkness, in some cases murder, etc. Vampires can provide some pretty easy flow of essence to said spirits, and I doubt they will want the Uratha to come in and wipe out their food supply. I also think you are underestimating vampires, by a lot. Kindred can wake up when their havens are attacked, and there are various ways for the Kindred to survive said attack. Then you have the mortal occultists that deal with spirits that could find ways to ward a vampire's haven. Beyond that, Cruac and Theban Sorcery can help even the edge against spirit magic because of their raw power alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:26:29-07:00","id":1133878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133871#post1133871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the Iron Masters are one of the Tribes, yes temporal influence does matter. And for the Shadow, there will be spirits that will fight alongside the Kindred. Spirits of paranoia, blood, darkness, in some cases murder, etc. Vampires can provide some pretty easy flow of essence to said spirits, and I doubt they will want the Uratha to come in and wipe out their food supply. I also think you are underestimating vampires, by a lot. Kindred can wake up when their havens are attacked, and there are various ways for the Kindred to survive said attack. Then you have the mortal occultists that deal with spirits that could find ways to ward a vampire's haven. Beyond that, Cruac and Theban Sorcery can help even the edge against spirit magic because of their raw power alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ward from what? Influence use? Raise the Gauntlet? Cahalith can howl and unmake it, then play Final Destination Death. The kind of spirits that benefit off vampiric predation are drones at most, without the intellectual acumen to realize what is going to happen, unless they actually actively influence kindred already, at which point it's a matter of merely dealing with those spirits as proxy. And if they want essence? Give them a locus to their liking with a merit.<br /> <br /> Regarding Iron Master's ties to a community? They don't get merits like allies and contacts the conventional way: they cheat with the same kind of spiritual tricks. They're more apt at ruining those resources in their prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-25-2017, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:28:12-07:00","id":1133880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133868#post1133868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. LOL no. They explicitly do not. It requires an expenditure of WP in order to give such an effect.<br /> <br /> 2. Your cognitive preference are dully noted.<br /> <br /> 3. Mass embrace a pack of murderous quasi revenants. Sure that'll be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Okay, kindred bleed when using the blush of life, which does not cost willpower. I don't know where you got that from.<br /> <br /> 3. They aren't Revenants. They are explicitly stated to be at BP 1. Page 159 of vampire the requiem, the Mass Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:33:08-07:00","id":1133885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133871#post1133871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the Iron Masters are one of the Tribes, yes temporal influence does matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Masters are not obligated to be a part of a city and can exist freely and fine the middle of a desert, hunting things totally unrelated to humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And for the Shadow, there will be spirits that will fight alongside the Kindred. Spirits of paranoia, blood, darkness, in some cases murder, etc. </div> </div> </div>Unlikely to the extreme. More likely the vampires would be claimed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires can provide some pretty easy flow of essence to said spirits, and I doubt they will want the Uratha to come in and wipe out their food supply. </div> </div> </div>You can kill all the vampires you want, it won't get rid of any spirits that aren't vampire spirits. And considering vampires 'at peace' aren't really generating much Essence they would likely prefer there to be some pressure. And obviously blood, murder, darkness and paranoia spirits can be just as easily fed by werewolves. Especially if they're preying on vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think you are underestimating vampires, by a lot. Kindred can wake up when their havens are attacked, and there are various ways for the Kindred to survive said attack. </div> </div> </div>They could also not wake up. Or they could awaken and be unable to do anything against a pack of werewolves even though they are awake. Mechanically it's more likely that they would wake up, then fall asleep again a few turns later.<br /> <br /> Really? We've already established and accepted vampires as a threat, beyond the rare fire-controlling werewolf. You seem to be willfully underestimating werewolves. However literally minded you are, you can see that the book posits Influences as not a literal hard-and-fact system to begin with. This does not mean that these things do not work. It means you don't want them to work the way the book suggests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you have the mortal occultists that deal with spirits that could find ways to ward a vampire's haven. Beyond that, Cruac and Theban Sorcery can help even the edge against spirit magic because of their raw power alone. </div> </div> </div>Cruac has some influence in the spirit, but if you're having occultists that would help vampires they would be balanced out by occultists that would help werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:35:06-07:00","id":1133888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133880#post1133880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Okay, kindred bleed when using the blush of life, which does not cost willpower. I don't know where you got that from.<br /> <br /> 3. They aren't Revenants. They are explicitly stated to be at BP 1. Page 159 of vampire the requiem, the Mass Embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blush of life fake blood isn't vitae, we can agree on that.<br /> <br /> Pseudo revenants as in, they go fucking crazy with blood hunger. Like sharks at the womb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:41:19-07:00","id":1133892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133878#post1133878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ward from what? Influence use? Raise the Gauntlet? Cahalith can howl and unmake it, then play Final Destination Death. The kind of spirits that benefit off vampiric predation are drones at most, without the intellectual acumen to realize what is going to happen, unless they actually actively influence kindred already, at which point it's a matter of merely dealing with those spirits as proxy. And if they want essence? Give them a locus to their liking with a merit.<br /> <br /> Regarding Iron Master's ties to a community? They don't get merits like allies and contacts the conventional way: they cheat with the same kind of spiritual tricks. They're more apt at ruining those resources in their prey.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Where exactly do Cahalith get the ability to howl and unmake the Gauntlet? It is not listed under the Moon Gift, and it's not under one of their starting gifts, so where did you get the Cahalith unmaking the Gauntlet aspect from?<br /> <br /> For the Iron Masters, just because you're good at shutting other people down does not mean you shouldn't have connections of your own. i don't see why an Iron Master wouldn't have mortal connections; it makes the Hunt far more advantageous for them.<br /> <br /> As for spiritual powers, we run into the issue of spiritual tricks going off a the werewolf's renown. it is unlikely you'll find many Uratha with high amounts of renown, just like it is unlikely you find Kindred with large levels of disciplines. Downplaying merits and mortal connections doesn't make a lot of sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:44:40-07:00","id":1133893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133888#post1133888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pseudo revenants as in, they go fucking crazy with blood hunger. Like sharks at the womb.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, they go into hunger frenzies typically because of the one vitae in their system (and the fact they need to roll a chance die to resist frenzy). A Kindred can (and hopefully will) prepare for that. The frenzy doesn't last forever though, unless they get a dramatic failure on the roll.<br /> <br /> Vampires are perfectly capable at getting desperate, and if they get desperate enough I could see some taking the chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T13:10:43-07:00","id":1133919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133892#post1133892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Iron Masters, just because you're good at shutting other people down does not mean you shouldn't have connections of your own. i don't see why an Iron Master wouldn't have mortal connections; it makes the Hunt far more advantageous for them.<br /> <br /> As for spiritual powers, we run into the issue of spiritual tricks going off a the werewolf's renown. it is unlikely you'll find many Uratha with high amounts of renown, just like it is unlikely you find Kindred with large levels of disciplines. Downplaying merits and mortal connections doesn't make a lot of sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get all relative with us now. You know how Uratha cheat the deal with &quot;spirit powers are only as useful as their renown&quot;? Talens granting the facet at 3 or more dots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T13:19:21-07:00","id":1133921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133919#post1133919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Get all relative with us now. You know how Uratha cheat the deal with &amp;quot;spirit powers are only as useful as their renown&amp;quot;? Talens granting the facet at 3 or more dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, so Uratha can cheat that aspect. I'm honestly tired of arguing for vampires at this point, so I'm bowing out of this thread now. Y'all have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T14:54:54-07:00","id":1133952,"title":"","content":"Said I was bowing out, but I hate the idea of being rude and ignoring people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1133885#post1133885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Iron Masters are not obligated to be a part of a city and can exist freely and fine the middle of a desert, hunting things totally unrelated to humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, I wouldn't play an Iron Master in this situation, but fair call.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unlikely to the extreme. More likely the vampires would be claimed. </div> </div> </div>Also a fair point, admittedly my knowledge of spirits sucks because I don't get to play werewolf often.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can kill all the vampires you want, it won't get rid of any spirits that aren't vampire spirits. And considering vampires 'at peace' aren't really generating much Essence they would likely prefer there to be some pressure. And obviously blood, murder, darkness and paranoia spirits can be just as easily fed by werewolves. Especially if they're preying on vampires. </div> </div> </div>You are admittedly right. I'm not well versed in spirit stuff, so I should probably just shut up about it and stick to vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They could also not wake up. Or they could awaken and be unable to do anything against a pack of werewolves even though they are awake. Mechanically it's more likely that they would wake up, then fall asleep again a few turns later. </div> </div> </div>I was referring to the Haven merit, which provides a mechanical bonus to waking up. Sure, if I'm the one playing the vampire I'm absolutely going to fail that roll, but that doesn't mean everyone will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really? We've already established and accepted vampires as a threat, beyond the rare fire-controlling werewolf. You seem to be willfully underestimating werewolves. However literally minded you are, you can see that the book posits Influences as not a literal hard-and-fact system to begin with. This does not mean that these things do not work. It means you don't want them to work the way the book suggests. </div> </div> </div>For influence, I said when I mentioned it that second time because I didn't see it working that way didn't mean it didn't work that way. I admitted that was probably the rules, and I just didn't connect the dots.<br /> <br /> And I don't underestimate werewolves. Werewolves are an objectively better species, and have a lot more advantages. I just felt like stepping in for vampire because that is what I mostly get to play.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cruac has some influence in the spirit, but if you're having occultists that would help vampires they would be balanced out by occultists that would help werewolves. </div> </div> </div>Also a fair point. I just wanted to point out that vampires had some occult capabilities to back them up in this case.<br /> <br /> However, like I said, I should bow out of this discussion. Not my place to do so. So, once more, y'all have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":". 08-26-2017, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T11:50:30-07:00","id":1134205,"title":"","content":"Everyone is acting like it's super easy for werewolves to get spirits to do what they want. Sure if a vampires haven is in the territory belonging to that particular pack of werewolves then yes, they likely have established spirit allies and will likely have an easy time ousting that particular kindred.<br /> ,l<br /> But that isn't the threat of dealing with vampires as a werewolf pack. Congratulations you toasted some vampires in your territory. But you didn't realize they were important members of the Circle of the Crone and they aren't all loacted in your territory by far. <br /> <br /> The crone use bullshit blood magic and now know who and what the killers are. Worst yet, you have trouble striking back against these kindred as they veil their havens with magic and some power they refer to as 'Obfuscate'. More importantly these hidden havens are located in other packs territories. Now everytime the Crone make some probing strike to your territory you have to negotiate with other packs to use their territory to hunt these kindred, or else try to do so without their permission. On these territories your pack has no established spirit allies, so coaxing favors from a fire spirit powerful enough to do any damage to a particular kindred haven requires copious amounts of essence or a favor to the spirit, and that's assuming the crone aren't now taking precautions against such attacks after divining what happened to your packs previous victims.<br /> <br /> Dealing with Kindred can bring the resources of an entire covenant against your pack. And a werewolf pack often will have only the packmates and any allies they have cultivated in their territory to aid them. <br /> <br /> Werewolves and Vampires both would have a difficult time with the other. Their is no clear winner I'd they go to war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","user":"Heroofthemists","date":". 08-26-2017, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T20:11:36-07:00","id":1134335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134205#post1134205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone is acting like it's super easy for werewolves to get spirits to do what they want. Sure if a vampires haven is in the territory belonging to that particular pack of werewolves then yes, they likely have established spirit allies and will likely have an easy time ousting that particular kindred.<br /> ,l<br /> But that isn't the threat of dealing with vampires as a werewolf pack. Congratulations you toasted some vampires in your territory. But you didn't realize they were important members of the Circle of the Crone and they aren't all loacted in your territory by far.<br /> <br /> The crone use bullshit blood magic and now know who and what the killers are. Worst yet, you have trouble striking back against these kindred as they veil their havens with magic and some power they refer to as 'Obfuscate'. More importantly these hidden havens are located in other packs territories. Now everytime the Crone make some probing strike to your territory you have to negotiate with other packs to use their territory to hunt these kindred, or else try to do so without their permission. On these territories your pack has no established spirit allies, so coaxing favors from a fire spirit powerful enough to do any damage to a particular kindred haven requires copious amounts of essence or a favor to the spirit, and that's assuming the crone aren't now taking precautions against such attacks after divining what happened to your packs previous victims.<br /> <br /> Dealing with Kindred can bring the resources of an entire covenant against your pack. And a werewolf pack often will have only the packmates and any allies they have cultivated in their territory to aid them.<br /> <br /> Werewolves and Vampires both would have a difficult time with the other. Their is no clear winner I'd they go to war.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've literally made a protectorate in my game with the express Aspiration of toasting Kindred and Ghouls into extinction, precisely because the Circle was fucking with spiritual matters. Can you guess which ones were the first we hit? Yes, the Cronies (pun intended). It wasn't even hard. And no, if I have Elemental facets, I don't need to ask fire spirits input to torch the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T05:18:15-07:00","id":1134442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134335#post1134335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've literally made a protectorate in my game with the express Aspiration of toasting Kindred and Ghouls into extinction, precisely because the Circle was fucking with spiritual matters. Can you guess which ones were the first we hit? Yes, the Cronies (pun intended). It wasn't even hard. And no, if I have Elemental facets, I don't need to ask fire spirits input to torch the place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which surely got the response that was feasible from the kindred community. <br /> <br /> The standard thing with these comments and scenarios is the one-sidedness it comes with. Everyone has pretty good understanding of their main splat and the setting one plays in from the splats perspective. The other splats are relocated to plotpoints and enemies, their social structure and powers are not really put into a larger perspective. <br /> For instance, attacking in a blitzkrieg fashion and murdering one covenant in the city would get all other kindred in against their common foe. Mutual animosities aside, in a place where a foe can and is willing to murder an entire covenant means the others are at the same risk. And last time i checked, self-preservation is usually a common theme among the kindred.<br /> <br /> Like in every act of splat vs. splat scenario, imagining it was easy or how easy one splat has to kill or destroy another is to downplay frailties and drawbacks from one side and downplay or straight up ignoring the powers of the other splat.<br /> No I'm not saying they are on equal footing, but they are never compared without heavy bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T10:02:07-07:00","id":1134508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134442#post1134442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which surely got the response that was feasible from the kindred community.<br /> <br /> The standard thing with these comments and scenarios is the one-sidedness it comes with. Everyone has pretty good understanding of their main splat and the setting one plays in from the splats perspective. The other splats are relocated to plotpoints and enemies, their social structure and powers are not really put into a larger perspective.<br /> For instance, attacking in a blitzkrieg fashion and murdering one covenant in the city would get all other kindred in against their common foe. Mutual animosities aside, in a place where a foe can and is willing to murder an entire covenant means the others are at the same risk. And last time i checked, self-preservation is usually a common theme among the kindred.<br /> <br /> Like in every act of splat vs. splat scenario, imagining it was easy or how easy one splat has to kill or destroy another is to downplay frailties and drawbacks from one side and downplay or straight up ignoring the powers of the other splat.<br /> No I'm not saying they are on equal footing, but they are never compared without heavy bias.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires literally lose 8 to 12 of hours of the day sleeping. Arranging that blitzkrieg was easy. The rest was sending the ultimatum of why the covenant got murdered. Genocides are ineffective for the same reason you don't corner a wounded animal. After you've dealt with the ones who'd put up a fight, the ones who didn't run scared shitless sought out a compromise, then added another tradition: don't fuck with lupines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T10:33:25-07:00","id":1134515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134508#post1134508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires literally lose 8 to 12 of hours of the day sleeping. Arranging that blitzkrieg was easy. The rest was sending the ultimatum of why the covenant got murdered. Genocides are ineffective for the same reason you don't corner a wounded animal. After you've dealt with the ones who'd put up a fight, the ones who didn't run scared shitless sought out a compromise, then added another tradition: don't fuck with lupines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Q.E.D.<br /> <br /> <br /> (characters)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T11:36:54-07:00","id":1134533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134442#post1134442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, attacking in a blitzkrieg fashion and murdering one covenant in the city would get all other kindred in against their common foe. Mutual animosities aside, in a place where a foe can and is willing to murder an entire covenant means the others are at the same risk. And last time i checked, self-preservation is usually a common theme among the kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except... Kindred are notorious for internal strife and back-biting. If the Circle wasn't popular in the domain, the other Covenants might instead send <i>gift baskets</i> to the werewolves. Sure, they probably study just what happened and take measures to ensure it doesn't happen to them too, all the while smiling and talking of alliance.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, more data is needed about the setup other than &quot;Vampires vs Werewolves&quot;. Numbers, existing connections, high powered members, specialist members, preparation, etc. All of them can swing near any group vs group conflict in either direction. Even Mages could lose to Hunters with enough weighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T13:13:33-07:00","id":1134591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134533#post1134533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except... Kindred are notorious for internal strife and back-biting. If the Circle wasn't popular in the domain, the other Covenants might instead send <i>gift baskets</i> to the werewolves. Sure, they probably study just what happened and take measures to ensure it doesn't happen to them too, all the while smiling and talking of alliance.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, more data is needed about the setup other than &quot;Vampires vs Werewolves&quot;. Numbers, existing connections, high powered members, specialist members, preparation, etc. All of them can swing near any group vs group conflict in either direction. Even Mages could lose to Hunters with enough weighting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes they are, but so is werewolves as well. But back to point, yes backstabbing fangs is kinda the trademark of vampires. I do although believe quite frankly that animosities will take the backseat for a while, not stop, just take the backseat if the rules of engagement changes so drastically that no one is safe anymore. As pointed out before, splat-societies, powers and influence must be taken more into these considerations, and as you as well point out be taking with more thought then just numbers.<br /> <br /> Yes, many vampires, notably the Lancea et Sanctum would probably rejoice that the cronies are gone, but that doesn't stop them from realizing that their heads are next. If something can and is willing to arbitrary wipe a whole covenant in a domain from the face of the earth, it's time for the other covenants to respond in kind and prepare.<br /> <br /> The idea that werewolves could wipe a covenant form the domain, &quot;easy&quot; is just either childish or just plain ignorant of the complexity of both the setting and reality (although i guess a pulpy or gonzo kind of playstyle/setting does allow for this) and does not conform to the basics of the cold war mentality that exists between and sometimes in-between splats.<br /> <br /> One way or another, a war between splats is a catastrophe of M.A.D. proportions in worst case or extremely taxing in the best of cases.<br /> <br /> Not even mages has a win-button.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":".  Just want to clarify that this whole post ain't pointed to you @Vent0 08-27-2017, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:11:30-07:00","id":1134602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134591#post1134591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes they are, but so is werewolves as well. But back to point, yes backstabbing fangs is kinda the trademark of vampires. I do although believe quite frankly that animosities will take the backseat for a while, not stop, just take the backseat if the rules of engagement changes so drastically that no one is safe anymore. As pointed out before, splat-societies, powers and influence must be taken more into these considerations, and as you as well point out be taking with more thought then just numbers.<br /> <br /> Yes, many vampires, notably the Lancea et Sanctum would probably rejoice that the cronies are gone, but that doesn't stop them from realizing that their heads are next. If something can and is willing to arbitrary wipe a whole covenant in a domain from the face of the earth, it's time for the other covenants to respond in kind and prepare.<br /> <br /> The idea that werewolves could wipe a covenant form the domain, &quot;easy&quot; is just either childish or just plain ignorant of the complexity of both the setting and reality (although i guess a pulpy or gonzo kind of playstyle/setting does allow for this) and does not conform to the basics of the cold war mentality that exists between and sometimes in-between splats.<br /> <br /> One way or another, a war between splats is a catastrophe of M.A.D. proportions in worst case or extremely taxing in the best of cases.<br /> <br /> Not even mages has a win-button.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that Werewolves are made to hunt, and the protectorate was created in order to keep the vampires in check. That dissuades the &quot;inner strife&quot; angle you're advocating there. It's their jam. Vampires would rather scurry to their havens every night for the next century than deal with a Prince machinations or an elder's agenda. Do let me know however the kindred would learn how to respond to the sort of unseen threat a pack implement with just Catastrophe and Tongue of Flame, without the Circle's eyes on the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:20:35-07:00","id":1134608,"title":"","content":"Sure, werewolf packs are famous for their backstabbing. And if Requiem for Rome has taught us anything, it's that vampires will put aside personal issues for the survival of the rest of their kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T16:14:17-07:00","id":1134652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134608#post1134608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, werewolf packs are famous for their backstabbing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf packs in plural \u2014 which is what the comparable element to covenants are in this context \u2014 are notorious for being a bunch of busybodies who will make a grab for someone else's territory at the first sign of weakness because they think they can do everybody's job better regardless of the actual situation. Stow the sarcasm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134602#post1134602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do let me know however the kindred would learn how to respond to the sort of unseen threat a pack implement with just Catastrophe and Tongue of Flame, without the Circle's eyes on the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing about Havens: They're built off of Safe Place and specifically build their scaling on how well-defended the place is against the sun, and they're often in cities. <i>Finding</i> a vampire's Haven, much less getting using Influence over fire from across the Gauntlet \u2014 on a place inhabited by a creature who doesn't need light to see, which might well be <i>underground</i> \u2014 is not going to be a walk in the park without a fairly specific set of competencies.<br /> <br /> If you've got a Purity 4 Ithaeur Hunter in Darkness poking around the sewer lair of a Nosferatu with high Obfuscate, that's pitting a veteran hunter against a veteran survivor, not the dismissive shenanigan of &quot;I'll just firebomb them from the Shadow.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T16:55:54-07:00","id":1134661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134591#post1134591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes they are, but so is werewolves as well. But back to point, yes backstabbing fangs is kinda the trademark of vampires. I do although believe quite frankly that animosities will take the backseat for a while, not stop, just take the backseat if the rules of engagement changes so drastically that no one is safe anymore. As pointed out before, splat-societies, powers and influence must be taken more into these considerations, and as you as well point out be taking with more thought then just numbers.<br /> <br /> Yes, many vampires, notably the Lancea et Sanctum would probably rejoice that the cronies are gone, but that doesn't stop them from realizing that their heads are next. If something can and is willing to arbitrary wipe a whole covenant in a domain from the face of the earth, it's time for the other covenants to respond in kind and prepare.<br /> <br /> The idea that werewolves could wipe a covenant form the domain, &quot;easy&quot; is just either childish or just plain ignorant of the complexity of both the setting and reality (although i guess a pulpy or gonzo kind of playstyle/setting does allow for this) and does not conform to the basics of the cold war mentality that exists between and sometimes in-between splats.<br /> <br /> One way or another, a war between splats is a catastrophe of M.A.D. proportions in worst case or extremely taxing in the best of cases.<br /> <br /> Not even mages has a win-button.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134602#post1134602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is that Werewolves are made to hunt, and the protectorate was created in order to keep the vampires in check. That dissuades the &quot;inner strife&quot; angle you're advocating there. It's their jam. Vampires would rather scurry to their havens every night for the next century than deal with a Prince machinations or an elder's agenda. Do let me know however the kindred would learn how to respond to the sort of unseen threat a pack implement with just Catastrophe and Tongue of Flame, without the Circle's eyes on the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134652#post1134652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf packs in plural \u2014 which is what the comparable element to covenants are in this context \u2014 are notorious for being a bunch of busybodies who will make a grab for someone else's territory at the first sign of weakness because they think they can do everybody's job better regardless of the actual situation. Stow the sarcasm.<br /> <br /> Funny thing about Havens: They're built off of Safe Place and specifically build their scaling on how well-defended the place is against the sun, and they're often in cities. <i>Finding</i> a vampire's Haven, much less getting using Influence over fire from across the Gauntlet \u2014 on a place inhabited by a creature who doesn't need light to see, which might well be <i>underground</i> \u2014 is not going to be a walk in the park without a fairly specific set of competencies.<br /> <br /> If you've got a Purity 4 Ithaeur Hunter in Darkness poking around the sewer lair of a Nosferatu with high Obfuscate, that's pitting a veteran hunter against a veteran survivor, not the dismissive shenanigan of &quot;I'll just firebomb them from the Shadow.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, all this just illustrates that it depends on more details than just &quot;Vampires vs Werewolves&quot;. If Werewolves are initiating hostilities without the Kindred knowing, they could indeed probably scout out many of the Vampires' Havens (Uratha have far too many tools to track undetected) and then firebomb them from the Shadow, etc. On the other hand, Vampires opening up the fight could set up an entire web of influence to destroy the Uratha's human lives and Pack members before they know what's coming. If the Covenant in question is small and disliked, they are probably better off gone, in most Vampires' minds. Conversely, if the Forsaken are small and disliked by the Spirit world, Kindred will find their efforts encouraged.<br /> <br /> Details matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T17:40:19-07:00","id":1134677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134652#post1134652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf packs in plural \u2014 which is what the comparable element to covenants are in this context \u2014 are notorious for being a bunch of busybodies who will make a grab for someone else's territory at the first sign of weakness because they think they can do everybody's job better regardless of the actual situation. Stow the sarcasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>They really aren't, though. It was pushed in first edition but it hasn't come up in second. In fact in second edition we've had more examples of werewolves banding together against threats to themselves, or just for general peace. The only time they've been seen turning against an established comfort level is when driven mad by an outside force.<br /> <br /> You don't have a trademark on sarcasm, Satchel. There's a reason werewolves have had the eight tribes for thousands of years and vampires go through covenants like they go through ghouls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Funny thing about Havens: They're built off of Safe Place and specifically build their scaling on how well-defended the place is against the sun, and they're often in cities. <i>Finding</i> a vampire's Haven, much less getting using Influence over fire from across the Gauntlet \u2014 on a place inhabited by a creature who doesn't need light to see, which might well be <i>underground</i> \u2014 is not going to be a walk in the park without a fairly specific set of competencies. </div> </div> </div>Or just general watching their territory. The ideal force to wipe out vampires is an Ivory Claw with Tongue of Flame, sure, I've said this repeatedly. Sacred hunt to locate connections, flame to burn them out. But most werewolves are going to do fine on their own.<br /> <br /> If you don't have that, you have to do some legwork, but werewolves are great at locating things, especially in their territory. Scent the Unnatural, Lore of the Land, just looking around. For the fraction of vampires that have hidden underground lairs, there's a fraction of werewolves that have Moldywarp, there was even a lodge built around the idea.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, they do need light to see. They're better at it than humans, but in full darkness they still have a penalty when relying on vision.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't need a defender here, we've already established this. Look at wyrdhamster's werewolf getting disarmed, literally, by a coterie of vampires. As Vent0 has said, it depends heavily on your setup. Until you specify some exact werewolves and vampires, you're going to have people back and forth white rooming 'It's conceivably possible that this won't happen because of this other thing that might,' and lopsided contrivances for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-27-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T17:45:53-07:00","id":1134682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134652#post1134652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf packs in plural \u2014 which is what the comparable element to covenants are in this context \u2014 are notorious for being a bunch of busybodies who will make a grab for someone else's territory at the first sign of weakness because they think they can do everybody's job better regardless of the actual situation. Stow the sarcasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't be Wise or Honorable or even Glorious if that territorial dispute wasn't useful. Grabbing territory because you feel like, because it proves you're the man and not because someone let shit skip their turf to get to you is a waste of resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134652#post1134652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny thing about Havens: They're built off of Safe Place and specifically build their scaling on how well-defended the place is against the sun, and they're often in cities. <i>Finding</i> a vampire's Haven, much less getting using Influence over fire from across the Gauntlet \u2014 on a place inhabited by a creature who doesn't need light to see, which might well be <i>underground</i> \u2014 is not going to be a walk in the park without a fairly specific set of competencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Competencies which half a decent Irraka have. Pulling a stake out on someone from the Shadow is stupidly easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134652#post1134652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've got a Purity 4 Ithaeur Hunter in Darkness poking around the sewer lair of a Nosferatu with high Obfuscate, that's pitting a veteran hunter against a veteran survivor, not the dismissive shenanigan of &quot;I'll just firebomb them from the Shadow.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't need that. Earthquake the damned sewer. Bust a gas line, set it on fire. From the Shadow. Add some prophecy into the mix to learn if the target will be available if you want to minimize damage. Vampires would feel like they're in a Final Destination movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T18:09:31-07:00","id":1134688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134677#post1134677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They really aren't, though. It was pushed in first edition but it hasn't come up in second. In fact in second edition we've had more examples of werewolves banding together against threats to themselves, or just for general peace.</div> </div> </div> </div>A greater emphasis on protectorates will do that, but it's no more an immunity to internal strife among a locale's packs than the selfish monster at the heart of vampirism is an invalidation of that species' institutional inertia.<br /> <br /> Vampire groups haven't historically had straightforward backing from extradimensional immortals directly descended from one of the most powerful beings in history. &quot;The tribes have been around a long time and there have been a lot of shorter-lived covenants&quot; doesn't mean much for unity when you remember that covenants don't have statless undying backers from another world propping them up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the fraction of vampires that have hidden underground lairs, there's a fraction of werewolves that have Moldywarp, there was even a lodge built around the idea. </div> </div> </div>And they'll do great at digging up a hidden vampire, but <i>the specific thing I was addressing was &quot;just firebomb them from across the Gauntlet.</i>&quot; I have no tolerance for that kind of reductive presentation of how mages interact with crossover complications and I see no reason to tacitly encourage it from the Werewolf boards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, they do need light to see. They're better at it than humans, but in full darkness they still have a penalty when relying on vision. </div> </div> </div>-2 is a middle-of-the-road expression of difficulty for the typical range of penalties a normal action will see. That's quite far from &quot;they actually need light to see.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As Vent0 has said, it depends heavily on your setup. Until you specify some exact werewolves and vampires, you're going to have people back and forth white rooming 'It's conceivably possible that this won't happen because of this other thing that might,' and lopsided contrivances for some reason. </div> </div> </div>My contention is that this means there is no real point in bringing those lopsided contrivances into a thread whose original question was a general one, much less arguing in defense of them and continuing to pin this thread to the front page. Answering the questions contrived setups present is one of the reasons we have games, not the job of bad-faith forum discussions about how Cunning 5 Irraka with Essence to burn are everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T18:10:03-07:00","id":1134689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134682#post1134682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't need that. Earthquake the damned sewer. Bust a gas line, set it on fire. From the Shadow. Add some prophecy into the mix to learn if the target will be available if you want to minimize damage. Vampires would feel like they're in a Final Destination movie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or just use blood magic to kill every werewolf in a 10 mile radius. Once again, white room scenarios are pointless and doesn't lead anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T18:26:08-07:00","id":1134697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1134688#post1134688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My contention is that this means there is no real point in bringing those lopsided contrivances into a thread whose original question was a general one, much less arguing in defense of them and continuing to pin this thread to the front page. Answering the questions contrived setups present is one of the reasons we have games, not the job of bad-faith forum discussions about how Cunning 5 Irraka with Essence to burn are everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Satchel has spoken everyone! we should get this thread locked. No, seriously. Beating a dead horse by now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T15:26:42-07:00","id":1135961,"title":"","content":"I would compare it to humans and Grizzly bears, a human would not hunt a grizzly by engaging in hand to hand combat, he would set traps, use guns, use spears, and any advantage to kill the bear without getting mauled in the process. I would apply the same principle to werewolves. Don't pick a fight and expect to win in hand to hand combat. So here is how I would assume that Vampires would fight<br /> <br /> 1/ Silver weapons, could be improvised, silver rings (brass knuckles?), clubs with silver on them, bullets with silver tips (should work), Shotguns with silver shot (which is sold on the internet)<br /> 2/ Dominate them from a distance and try to control them before the fight starts<br /> 3/ Send ghouls to attack on your behalf with heavy weapons<br /> 4/ Use Obfuscate to hit them in an ambush when they are not ready and slay them in one strike<br /> 5/ Let them go into Basu-Ilm, use Celerity to get away, then come back when they are exhausted in their human forms...<br /> <br /> The possibilities are endless, all it takes is imagination","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T03:33:33-07:00","id":1136131,"title":"","content":"Everytime this discussion comes up it seems that everyone is full of heavy weapons and silver( with the chance to get them in one turn) to organize a war party of heavy armored ghouls.<br /> <br /> <b>If</b> a pack of uratha/anshega is <b>on the hunt for your coterie</b> you are 99% dead meat. Take a look to the 2nd ed forms powers, gifts, rituals, and think about an entire pack stalking you.<br /> And entire pack of social werewolves if you want. <br /> <br /> <u>Welcome to reality.</u><br /> <br /> <br /> If you are a werewolf-hunting coterie, well, things can change. Vampires are predators too. Good luck when you will hunt the wrong pack. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T03:55:24-07:00","id":1136133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1135961#post1135961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would compare it to humans and Grizzly bears, a human would not hunt a grizzly by engaging in hand to hand combat, he would set traps, use guns, use spears, and any advantage to kill the bear without getting mauled in the process. I would apply the same principle to werewolves. Don't pick a fight and expect to win in hand to hand combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but you are wrong completely. Cuz in this case &quot;Grizzlies&quot; as clever as &quot;humans&quot;. Really, where this 'all werewolves are dumb' came from? That's racist)) (And, r<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">eally, for me it sounds rude<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</span><br /> I DON'T tell that you methods won't wok. But:<br /> 1) They are neither easy nor<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> garantie win.<br /> 2) Werewolves has the same 'endless possibilities, all it takes is imagination'<br /> I think, generally (considering all abilities), vampires and werewolves are equals in CoD. It's not true blood where it was like that:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kbUrJtflv1M&amp;t=4s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kbUrJtflv1M&amp;t=4s</a><br /> and where werewolves deserved such attitude.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 09-01-2017, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T04:34:35-07:00","id":1136137,"title":"","content":"I don't see where they implied werewolves are dumb. <br /> <br /> &quot;Imagine a grizzly bear, but even stronger and more resilient, and with the intelligence of a human. And magic. That's what you're dealing with.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T05:12:50-07:00","id":1136144,"title":"","content":"I answered to this. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would compare it to humans and <b>Grizzly bears</b>, a human would not hunt a grizzly by engaging in hand to hand combat, he would <b>set traps, use guns, use spears, and any advantage to kill the bear without getting mauled in the process</b>. </div> </div> </div> Sounds like the author forgot part about &quot;inteleence'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T05:48:20-07:00","id":1136147,"title":"","content":"I think the focus was more on the &quot;not in hand-to-hand combat&quot; bit. <br /> <br /> Humans can fall for traps. The underlying principle of &quot;fight smarter&quot; is still there. It's just more difficult because smarter than a werewolf is a lot higher bar than smarter than a bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T07:07:51-07:00","id":1136172,"title":"","content":"There's Gifts that makes things like ambushes and traps useless. That's why whiterooms don't work. Unless you determine the exact capabilities of everyone involved this has no point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T07:22:45-07:00","id":1136182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1136172#post1136172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's why whiterooms don't work. Unless you determine the exact capabilities of everyone involved this has no point.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. But outside of white room any comparison makes no sense. Cuz it's always about &quot;what IF we'll fight them with silver and ghouls&quot; &quot;what if we'll fight them with fire and at day&quot; &quot;what if-what if-what if<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T08:12:18-07:00","id":1136196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1136182#post1136182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yep. But outside of white room any comparison makes no sense. Cuz it's always about &quot;what IF we'll fight them with silver and ghouls&quot; &quot;what if we'll fight them with fire and at day&quot; &quot;what if-what if-what if</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Basically this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/WTDnnwE.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T08:31:23-07:00","id":1136200,"title":"","content":"New idea: Vampires and Werewolves vs This Fucking Trope.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://images.uncyc.org/pt/3/3d/Civility.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T08:39:22-07:00","id":1136201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1136137#post1136137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see where they implied werewolves are dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general thrust of the thread has had vampires running around with silver weaponry, setting traps and having amassed legions of ghouls trained in combat and wielding silver waiting for the werewolves to just charge at them from across the street at midnight. Basically every 'a werewolf could do this,' has been countered by, 'but vampires would be prepared for that,' or 'silly werewolves can't manage that.'<br /> <br /> I mentioned a couple times vampires didn't really need a champion here. It's because this thread has happened before, twice. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607632#post607632\">They even set parameters for the vampire and werewolf, and showed the math</a>. There was another thread that did it as well, but I've lost it. Plus people have been trying to give werewolf the shaft since before the game came out, not wanting them to have Lethal claw and fang against people with basic resistances. Werewolf's been on the defense regarding the 'versus' question for years, and attackers come out of the woodwork. Maybe it's an Apocalypse thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-01-2017, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T09:12:21-07:00","id":1136207,"title":"","content":"^^^ This. In such threads some people always try to humilate werewolves (and exactly werewolves neither mages, demons, changelings, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T09:18:16-07:00","id":1136209,"title":"","content":"Ghoul thing wouldn't work, anyway. They're not immune to lunacy, so werewolves have a few ways to make them shit themselves and scatter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T09:22:51-07:00","id":1136210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1136209#post1136209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They're not immune to lunacy</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't they? I though any supernatural template is immune by default.<br /> From the other hand, ghouls don't seem tough enough to be immune to Dawn and Dirty combat. And to bullets)))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T09:32:23-07:00","id":1136215,"title":"","content":"Anything that <i>doesn't have integrity</i> is immune. And also wolfblooded because that's one of their specific bennies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T09:52:16-07:00","id":1136223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1136147#post1136147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the focus was more on the &quot;not in hand-to-hand combat&quot; bit.<br /> <br /> Humans can fall for traps. The underlying principle of &quot;fight smarter&quot; is still there. It's just more difficult because smarter than a werewolf is a lot higher bar than smarter than a bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct sir. The point was engaging in hand to hand combat. In addition, I figured that once werewolves enter their war forms, and especially in Basu-Ilm, most reason goes out the window so that is where the analogy of a raging grizzly bear comes from. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T10:22:04-07:00","id":1136238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1136209#post1136209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghoul thing wouldn't work, anyway. They're not immune to lunacy, so werewolves have a few ways to make them shit themselves and scatter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except that Lunacy kicks in after the encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T10:25:12-07:00","id":1136240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1136238#post1136238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Lunacy kicks in after the encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunacy <i>can </i>kick in after the encounter. It can kick in immediately, as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T21:48:02-07:00","id":1136493,"title":"","content":"The problem with vampires vs. werewolves is that the outcome changes based on xp levels.<br /> A starting werewolf will most likely defeat a starting vampire, in mid-level it's equal, and at high end the vampire wins. If the vampire somehow neutralizes Gauru (such as by going invisible and outlasting the timer, or simply staying out of reach), the vampire wins from mid-level onward.<br /> <br /> The problems really arise in that vampires have some nice things that scale with blood potency. Those are Frenzy benefits (increased by going Wyrm-Ordo), and vitae expenditure. These two combined will mean that a vampire can get high enough of a dice pool to take out the Uratha with relative ease. Vampires can also benefit from using large weapons, unlike the Uratha, whose damage increase ability is tied to their natural weapons. Vampires also have a few benefits that the Uratha lack. Such as a power to increase defence (two, if Wyrm-Ordo). If it's a group fight, the Uratha suffer as well, since their damage reduction power (Rage - Glory, Berserker's Might) only stops one instance of damage, whereas Resilience stops more, and works on all sources.<br /> <br /> For great defensive powers, the Uratha have cost on their side, but vampires have power and utility. Juggernaut's Gait is expensive, but it is complete immunity to damage, and as long as one can afford the great cost, it's use is unlimited. Gauru on the other hand has fantastic healing, but it does nothing to handle extreme amounts of damage. It is also limited in it's use. It has one burst, that lasts a few rounds. If the vampire can last that long, the fight is theirs. Kuruth on the other hand takes away the utility of the other shapes, which means that the werewolf is forced to rely on a single (though strong) path to victory.<br /> <br /> Gift of Elements (Purity) is a great counter for vampires, but Claws of the Unholy on the other hand are a great counter for everything.<br /> <br /> And honestly. I see no problem with this. Werewolves counter their weakness by being parts of packs who work well together. Vampires tend to get more and more lonely and mistrustful as they age, and won't really have anyone to rely on to watch their backs in combat. So yeah, werewolves lose one-on-one, but they rarely fight one-on-one either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T10:53:39-07:00","id":1136637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1136493#post1136493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with vampires vs. werewolves is that the outcome changes based on xp levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>But also time of day. I'd argue this has a much bigger impact.<br /> <br /> I mean, if a human can sneak into a vampire's lair and kill them while they sleep, a werewolf can do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T11:21:56-07:00","id":1136649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1114913-vampires-vs-werewolves?p=1136637#post1136637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if a human can sneak into a vampire's lair and kill them while they sleep, a werewolf can do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Far more easily, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}